msgid "The :guilabel:`Credentials` section, whose fields depend on the selected provider. Secrets such as private keys are only visible to the :guilabel:`Bank Sync / Admin` group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:107
msgid "The :guilabel:`Capabilities` section is filled in by the provider module and tells you what the connection supports: :guilabel:`Supports statement pull`, :guilabel:`Supports FX rates`, :guilabel:`Supports webhooks`, :guilabel:`Supports payouts` and :guilabel:`Supports consent redirect`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:112
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Test connection` to verify the credentials: a notification confirms that the provider answered, and if it refuses the credentials the reason is displayed in an error message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:115
msgid "The status bar shows where the connection stands. How a connection becomes :guilabel:`Connected` depends on the provider: with Wise, a successful :guilabel:`Test connection`; with Nyíltbankolás, the end of the pairing (:guilabel:`Refresh / discover`); with Enable Banking, the consent given at the bank. A failed bank authorization sets the status to :guilabel:`Error` and stores the reason in :guilabel:`Last error`. A connection whose consent has run out is set to :guilabel:`Expired` and must be renewed, see :ref:`accounting/bank-sync/consent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:135
msgid "Nyíltbankolás Partner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:137
msgid "The aggregator connects to the Hungarian banks on your behalf. Enter the :guilabel:`Nyíltbankolás entity id` and the :guilabel:`Nyíltbankolás API key` you received from the service, then click :guilabel:`Get connection code`. Odoo requests a connection code, which is displayed in the :guilabel:`Connection code` field: use it on the provider's site to authorize your bank accounts. Once the authorization is done, click :guilabel:`Refresh / discover`: the connection becomes :guilabel:`Connected` and the list of authorized accounts is pulled into Odoo. Requesting a new connection code sets the connection back to :guilabel:`Draft` until the pairing is finished again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:149
#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:37
msgid "Wise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:151
msgid "Enter the :guilabel:`Wise profile id` and the :guilabel:`Wise API token`. For payouts, Wise also requires a :guilabel:`Wise SCA RSA private key (PEM)` used to sign strong-customer-authentication challenges, and for webhook delivery the :guilabel:`Wise webhook public key (PEM)` published by Wise for the chosen environment. Use :guilabel:`Subscribe webhooks` to register Odoo with Wise so that new transactions trigger an immediate refresh, and :guilabel:`Unsubscribe webhooks` to stop them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:159
msgid "Webhook events are delivered to `/bank_sync/webhook/<provider>` on your database. Signature verification fails closed: an event that cannot be verified is rejected. Ask your system administrator to make sure this address is reachable from the internet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:166
msgid "Bank consent and expiry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:168
msgid "Providers that read your accounts through PSD2 (currently Enable Banking) do not use a password stored in Odoo. Instead, you give a **consent** at your bank, with the bank's own strong customer authentication. The :guilabel:`Bank consent` section of the connection, shown for such providers, holds the settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:173
msgid ":guilabel:`Account holder type`: :guilabel:`Business` (default) or :guilabel:`Personal`, the type of online banking login you use at the bank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:175
msgid ":guilabel:`Consent valid until`: the end of the consent. PSD2 allows at most 180 days, and a bank may grant less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:177
msgid ":guilabel:`Consent responsible`: the user who receives the renewal reminder (by default, the user who created the connection)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:179
msgid ":guilabel:`Remind days before expiry`: how many days ahead the reminder is created (7 by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:180
msgid ":guilabel:`Max. unattended syncs per day`: how many scheduled synchronizations the bank allows per account and day (see :ref:`accounting/bank-sync/run`). Enable Banking sets 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:183
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Connect to bank` to open the authorization page of the bank. When you come back to Odoo, the connection is :guilabel:`Connected` and :guilabel:`Consent valid until` is filled in. A message is logged in the chatter of the connection. If the authorization is refused or takes longer than an hour, an error page is displayed with a link back to the connections; start again with :guilabel:`Connect to bank`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:189
msgid "Once a day, the *Online Bank Sync: consent expiry reminder* scheduled action (enabled by default) does two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:192
msgid "when the consent is :guilabel:`Remind days before expiry` days from its end, it schedules a :guilabel:`Renew the bank consent` activity for the :guilabel:`Consent responsible`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:194
msgid "when the consent has ended, it sets the connection to :guilabel:`Expired` and logs a message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:196
msgid "An expired connection is not called any more: its accounts show the error *The bank consent expired on ...* until you click :guilabel:`Renew consent` and authorize again at the bank. The accounts, the journal mapping and the imported history are kept, and the next synchronization catches up from the last successful run (within what the bank still delivers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:204
msgid "Map the remote accounts to journals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:206
msgid "On a connected connection, click :guilabel:`Discover accounts`. Odoo queries the provider and creates one :guilabel:`Bank Sync Account` record per remote account or balance. Open :menuselection:`Accounting --> Bank Sync --> Accounts` and set, for each of them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:210
msgid ":guilabel:`Journal`: the bank journal in which the transactions are booked. **Nothing is imported until a journal is set.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:212
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync enabled`: activates the scheduled import for this account. It is off by default, also for the accounts discovered by a provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:214
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync every`: the polling interval (for example, 1 hour). For a provider with a daily call limit, Odoo never polls more often than the limit allows (every 6 hours for 4 calls a day)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:217
msgid "The list view shows :guilabel:`Last successful run` and a colored :guilabel:`Last state` badge (:guilabel:`OK`, :guilabel:`Running`, :guilabel:`Error`), so you can spot an account that has stopped importing at a glance. The optional :guilabel:`Balance difference` column belongs to the :ref:`balance check <accounting/bank-sync/balance-check>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:222
msgid "Once a journal is mapped, its :guilabel:`Bank Feeds` setting (:guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab of the journal) is set to :guilabel:`Online Bank Sync`, and the journal card of the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard` gets a :guilabel:`Sync now` button. Statement files can still be imported into the journal, see :ref:`accounting/bank/import-backfill`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:240
msgid "Run a synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:242
msgid "There are three ways a synchronization runs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:244
msgid "**Scheduled**: the *Online Bank Sync: pull statements* scheduled action checks every 15 minutes which accounts are due and imports them. This scheduled action is **disabled by default**; ask your system administrator to enable it once the mapping is in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:247
msgid "**Manual**: click :guilabel:`Sync now` on the account form, or on the journal card of the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`. Manual runs are made while you are present, so they do not use up the daily limit of the scheduled runs described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:250
msgid "**Webhook-triggered**: for providers supporting webhooks, an incoming event flags the account and the next scheduled run imports it immediately, even when periodic polling is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:253
msgid "Each run fetches the transactions since the last successful run, with a 48-hour overlap so that transactions the bank posts late are not missed. Importing is **idempotent**: a transaction already present in the journal is skipped, so running a synchronization twice never creates duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:258
msgid "A synchronization only looks back a short time before its first run. It does not load the history that precedes the connection: import it from a statement file, see :ref:`accounting/bank/import-backfill`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:262
msgid "**Daily limit of PSD2 banks.** PSD2 allows a bank to refuse more than 4 account requests a day when the customer is not present. When the connection has a value in :guilabel:`Max. unattended syncs per day`, the scheduled runs stop for the rest of the day (UTC) once that number is reached for an account, and resume the next day. Manual runs are not counted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:267
msgid "If a run fails, the account is set to :guilabel:`Error` and the message is stored in :guilabel:`Last error`; the other accounts are not affected. Credentials and tokens are removed from the stored messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:272
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync now` displays *Bank sync finished.* even when the run failed, because the error is recorded on the account instead of being raised. After a manual synchronization, check :guilabel:`Last state` and :guilabel:`Last error` on the account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:279
msgid "Balance check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:281
msgid "When the provider reports the balance of the account (Enable Banking does), every successful run compares the booked balance of the bank with the balance of the journal's bank account in your books, up to the date of the bank balance. Only posted entries count. The account form shows the result in the :guilabel:`Balance check` section (:guilabel:`Balance`, :guilabel:`Bank balance date`, :guilabel:`Accounting balance` and :guilabel:`Balance difference`, in red when it is not zero)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:287
msgid "When the two differ, the journal card of the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard` shows a :guilabel:`Balance differs` warning next to :guilabel:`Sync now`. The usual reasons are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:290
msgid "the balance of the account before the first imported transaction was never booked in Odoo. Post an opening balance entry in the journal's bank account;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:292
msgid "transactions are still missing, for example because the history was not back-filled;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:293
msgid "a transaction is still pending at the bank: Enable Banking only imports booked transactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:295
msgid "The check is a control, not a correction: nothing is booked automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:300
msgid "Outbound payouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/bank_synchronization.rst:302
msgid "Providers that support payouts (currently Wise) can also send money out of Odoo. Because this moves real funds, payouts are protected by a maker–checker workflow."
msgstr ""

