#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:6
msgid "Cash register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:8
msgid "The **Cash register** (*Házipénztár*) turns an Odoo cash journal into a Hungarian strict-accountability (*szigorú számadás*) cash book. Every cash movement becomes a numbered cash voucher (*pénztárbizonylat*), the vouchers are collected on cash-book pages that are closed with a serial number and locked, and each page prints as a cash report (*pénztárjelentés*) together with the cash count of the drawer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:14
msgid "The module builds on standard Odoo :ref:`cash journals <accounting/journals/cash>`, the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard` and the reconciliation view of the statement lines; it does not replace them, it extends them with the controls a strict-accountability cash book requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:19
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:21
msgid "In a cash journal, every cash movement is a statement line, and the journal entry of that line is the cash voucher: its number is the voucher number. A voucher can be recorded from three places (the cash journal card, the reconciliation view, or a payment), and in each case it is numbered, put on the open cash-book page and printed the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:27
msgid "Key features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:29
msgid "**Two numbering modes per cash journal**: one common series for receipts and disbursements, or two separate series (``BEF/`` for receipts, ``KIF/`` for disbursements). See :ref:`cash_register/numbering`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:32
msgid "**Gap-free, audit-proof vouchers**: an issued voucher can never be deleted. A wrong voucher is voided; it keeps its number and appears as voided on the cash report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:34
msgid "**Recording from anywhere**: a cash receipt or payment can be recorded from the cash journal card, from the reconciliation view, or by paying an invoice or bill in cash. See :ref:`cash_register/record`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:37
msgid "**Cash-book pages**: every cash voucher lands on the open page of its journal. Closing a page gives it a serial ``STAT`` number and locks it; only an accounting administrator can reopen it, and no voucher may be dated before a closed period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:40
msgid "**Cash report**: the printed page lists the opening balance, the vouchers with a running balance, daily totals, the voided vouchers, the closing balance, the last cash count and the signature lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:43
msgid "**Cash count with an optional controller**: the drawer is counted by denomination and compared with the book balance. A discrepancy needs a reason and the approval of an accounting administrator, and a cash journal can require a second user to check every count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:58
msgid "The Cash register is an *eYssen* extension for Hungarian localization. Once the cash journals are configured, day-to-day work (vouchers, pages, cash counts) is done from the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`."
msgstr ""

