#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:74
msgid "One running number for all vouchers of the cash desk, in the order they are recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:75
msgid "Two independent running numbers, one for receipts (*bevételi bizonylat*) and one for disbursements (*kiadási bizonylat*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:78
msgid "In the examples, ``PENZ`` is the short code of the cash journal and ``2026`` is the fiscal year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:80
msgid "Hungarian law does not prescribe either mode: the cash-handling policy (*pénzkezelési szabályzat*) of the company decides. Separate numbering follows the traditional pre-printed receipt and disbursement voucher pads; common numbering gives a single sequence that is easy to check for gaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:85
msgid "The numbering mode can only be changed at the start of a fiscal year. Once a voucher has been numbered in the current fiscal year, the setting can no longer be changed for that year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:87
msgid "With separate numbering, a voucher keeps its direction: an issued receipt cannot be turned into a disbursement (or the other way round) by changing its amount. Void it and record a new one instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:90
msgid "A line with a zero amount moves no cash and gets no ``BEF/`` or ``KIF/`` number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:91
msgid "Other entries of the cash journal that are not vouchers (for example a manual journal entry) keep the plain ``PENZ/`` numbering in both modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:95
msgid "When a cash voucher is issued for a payment (see :ref:`cash_register/record`), the payment keeps its own journal entry with a separate number (for example ``PPENZ/2026/00001``). The voucher number shown on the printed voucher and on the cash report is always the number of the cash voucher, not that of the payment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:103
msgid "Cash-book page numbering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:105
msgid "A closed cash-book page receives a gap-free ``STAT`` number. The module ships the :guilabel:`Cash Book - Statement` sequence (prefix ``STAT/``, restarting every year); select it, or your own copy of it, in the :guilabel:`Statement Sequence` field of each cash journal. A page cannot be closed until the journal has a :guilabel:`Statement Sequence`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:110
msgid "To create your own sequence, duplicate the supplied one in :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Sequences & Identifiers --> Sequences` and keep its :guilabel:`Implementation` set to :guilabel:`No gap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:115
#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments.rst:24
#: ../../content/applications/finance/payment_providers.rst:239
#: ../../content/applications/finance/payment_providers/nuvei.rst:51
#: ../../content/applications/finance/payment_providers/redsys.rst:85
msgid "Payment methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:117
msgid "When an invoice or a bill is paid with a cash journal, the payment is first booked against an outstanding account, and its cash voucher books the cash. On the :guilabel:`Incoming Payments` and :guilabel:`Outgoing Payments` tabs of the cash journal, the payment methods may therefore not use the cash account itself in the :guilabel:`Outstanding Receipts accounts` and :guilabel:`Outstanding Payments accounts` columns. Leave these columns empty to use the default outstanding accounts of the company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:124
msgid "A cash payment must also be in the currency of its cash journal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:129
msgid "Controller for the cash count"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:131
msgid "By default, the user who counts the drawer also closes the count. Tick :guilabel:`Controller Required for Cash Count` on a cash journal to apply the four-eyes principle: every count of that journal must then be checked and approved by a second user, the controller, before it closes. See :ref:`cash_register/cash-count` for the procedure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:136
msgid "The controller must be an active internal user of the company with accounting rights, and cannot be the user who counts the cash. Leave the option cleared on databases where only one user handles the cash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:3
msgid "Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:5
msgid "Day-to-day cash handling starts from the cash journal card of the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`. Its main button and its name open the reconciliation view of the cash journal, and the cash-register buttons sit next to the standard ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:21
msgid "Record a cash receipt or payment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:23
msgid "A cash voucher can be recorded from three places. Wherever it starts, the voucher is numbered, placed on the open cash-book page and printed the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:30
msgid "Where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:31
msgid "Use it for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:32
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:33
msgid "Cash journal card: :guilabel:`New Cash-in` or :guilabel:`New Cash-out`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:34
msgid "Everyday cash movements, whether or not an invoice belongs to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:35
msgid "The voucher is recorded; you then match it with an invoice or book it to an account in the reconciliation view, where it opens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:37
msgid "Reconciliation view: :guilabel:`New`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:38
msgid "The same, when you are already working in the reconciliation view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:39
msgid "The voucher is recorded and appears in the list, ready to be matched or booked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:40
msgid "Paying an invoice or a bill: :guilabel:`Pay` with the cash journal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:41
msgid "Settling a known invoice or bill in cash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:42
msgid "A payment is created, and its voucher is issued and matched automatically. Nothing else is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:45
msgid "A payment created by hand in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Customers --> Payments` or :menuselection:`Accounting --> Vendors --> Payments` with the cash journal works like the third case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:50
msgid "From the cash journal card"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:52
msgid "On the cash journal card, click :guilabel:`New Cash-in` for money received, or :guilabel:`New Cash-out` for money paid out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:54
msgid "Enter the :guilabel:`Date`, the :guilabel:`Label` (the title of the cash movement, *jogcím*), the :guilabel:`Partner` and the :guilabel:`Amount`. Enter the amount without a sign: the button gives the direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:57
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Save`. The voucher receives its number, lands on the open cash-book page, and the reconciliation view of the cash journal opens with the new voucher selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:59
msgid "Match the voucher with an open invoice or bill on the :guilabel:`Reconcile` tab, or book it to an account on the :guilabel:`Manual operation` tab, then click :guilabel:`Validate`. The voucher stays in the list after it is matched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:62
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Print Cash Voucher` to print the voucher. It can be printed as soon as it is recorded, before or after matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:76
msgid "From the reconciliation view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:78
msgid "Open the reconciliation view with the main button of the cash journal card, then click :guilabel:`New`. The form is the same as above, but here the sign of the :guilabel:`Amount` gives the direction: a positive amount is a receipt, a negative amount a disbursement. After saving, select the new voucher in the list to match, book and print it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:84
msgid "By paying an invoice or a bill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:86
msgid "On a posted invoice or bill, click :guilabel:`Pay`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:87
msgid "Select the cash journal as :guilabel:`Journal`, check the amount and the date, and click :guilabel:`Create Payment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:90
msgid "The payment is booked against an outstanding account, its cash voucher is issued in the cash journal and the two are matched at once, so the invoice is paid. The voucher can be printed from the reconciliation view of the cash journal with :guilabel:`Print Cash Voucher`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:95
msgid "While its cash voucher stands, the payment cannot be reset to draft, cancelled or deleted. To correct it, void the voucher first (see below), then change the payment; posting the payment again issues a new voucher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:100
msgid "Void a cash voucher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:102
msgid "An issued voucher can never be deleted, because its number must stay accountable. To void a wrong voucher (*rontás*), open its journal entry with :guilabel:`View move` in the reconciliation view and click :guilabel:`Cancel Entry`. The voucher keeps its number, no longer counts in the cash balance, and appears as **VOIDED** on the cash report. Record the correct movement as a new voucher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:107
msgid "A voucher on a closed cash-book page cannot be voided: reopen the page first, or record a correcting voucher dated today."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:113
msgid "Cash-book pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:115
msgid "A cash-book page (*pénztárjelentés-lap*) collects the vouchers of a period. Every new voucher lands automatically on the open page of its cash journal; when the journal has no open page, the first voucher opens a new one. A page is either :guilabel:`Open` or :guilabel:`Confirmed` (closed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:119
msgid "The pages of a cash journal are listed with :menuselection:`(cash journal card) ⋮ --> Cash Registers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:133
msgid "Close a cash-book page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:135
msgid "Close the page at the end of the period set in the cash-handling policy (for example every day or every month): select it in the list and choose :menuselection:`Action --> Confirm cash-book`. On closing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:139
msgid "The page receives the next gap-free :guilabel:`STAT Number` (for example ``STAT/2026/00013``). An open page never uses up a number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:141
msgid "The page is locked. No voucher can be added to it, its vouchers can no longer be changed (amount, date, partner, label, order) or voided, and its balances are fixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:143
msgid "The next voucher opens a new page, whose opening balance is the closing balance of this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:144
msgid "No new voucher may be dated before the last day of the closed pages. A voucher dated on that same day is allowed, so a page closed at midday can be followed by vouchers of the afternoon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:147
msgid "The bookkeeping of a voucher on a closed page can still be completed: for example, a voucher booked to a suspense or outstanding account can be matched with an invoice later. This does not change the cash report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:152
msgid "Reopen a cash-book page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:154
msgid "A closed page can be reopened with :menuselection:`Action --> Reopen cash-book`. Only users with the :guilabel:`Administrator` access right of :guilabel:`Accounting` can reopen a page. Reopening keeps the existing ``STAT`` number — a page is never renumbered — and is recorded in the chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:159
msgid "Print the cash report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:161
msgid "Open a cash-book page and choose :menuselection:`Print --> Cash Report`. The cash report (*pénztárjelentés*) shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:164
msgid "the company, the cash desk and its currency, the ``STAT`` number and the period of the page;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:165
msgid "the opening balance;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:166
msgid "every voucher in order, with its date, number, title, partner, receipt or disbursement and the running balance, and the voided vouchers marked **VOIDED** without an amount;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:168
msgid "the daily totals and the closing balance;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:169
msgid "the last approved cash count of the page with its denominations, or a note that no cash count was taken;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:171
msgid "signature lines for the cashier and the checker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:173
msgid "An open page can be printed too, for information: the report is then marked **NOT CLOSED - FOR INFORMATION ONLY** and has no ``STAT`` number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:179
msgid "Count the cash drawer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:181
msgid "To compare the physical cash with the books, click :guilabel:`Close Cash Register` on the cash journal card. Enter the number of coins and bills per denomination; the :guilabel:`Counted Balance` and the :guilabel:`Discrepancy` against the :guilabel:`Cash Balance in Journal` are computed as you type. The book balance is computed again from the journal at the moment the count is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:196
msgid "The next steps depend on the :guilabel:`Controller Required for Cash Count` setting of the cash journal (see :ref:`cash_register/controller`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:200
msgid "Without a controller (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:202
msgid "**No discrepancy**: click :guilabel:`Close`. The count is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:203
msgid "**Discrepancy**: enter the :guilabel:`Reason for Discrepancy` and click :guilabel:`Forward to the Manager`. The count waits for approval (:guilabel:`Waiting for Approval`) until an accounting administrator clicks :guilabel:`Close with Discrepancy`. When only one user handles the cash, that user may approve the own count, provided they have the :guilabel:`Administrator` access right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:209
msgid "With a controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:211
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Controller`: an active internal user of the company with accounting rights, other than yourself. If there is a discrepancy, enter the :guilabel:`Reason for Discrepancy` too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:213
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Send for Check`. The count is fixed as counted and waits for the controller (:guilabel:`Waiting for Check`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:215
msgid "The controller opens the count and clicks :guilabel:`Approve Count`. Only the selected controller can do this. Without a discrepancy the count is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:217
msgid "If there is a discrepancy, the count then waits for approval (:guilabel:`Waiting for Approval`), and an accounting administrator clicks :guilabel:`Close with Discrepancy`. The approver cannot be the user who counted the cash; the controller may be the same administrator, so two people are enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:223
msgid "After the count"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:225
msgid "The count belongs to the open cash-book page of the journal (to the last page, if the page was already closed), and the cash report of that page prints it once it is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:227
msgid "Once sent or closed, a count can no longer be changed; only a draft count can be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:228
msgid ":guilabel:`Print` produces the cash count sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:230
msgid "Past counts are listed under :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Cash Register Closures`, where they can be filtered by state (:guilabel:`Draft`, :guilabel:`Waiting for Check`, :guilabel:`Waiting for Approval`, :guilabel:`Closed`) and grouped by cash register, user or controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:3
msgid "Enable Banking (PSD2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:5
msgid "*Enable Banking* is an account information provider for the :doc:`online bank synchronization <bank_synchronization>`. It connects Odoo to the bank accounts of Spanish banks and of many other European banks, using the PSD2 interface every bank has to offer. You give a consent at your bank once, and Odoo then imports the booked transactions into the matching bank journal, several times a day, without you handing over your online banking password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:11
msgid "Use it when your bank does not offer a file export you want to upload every day, or when you manage many accounts and want the transactions and the balance check to be up to date on their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:15
msgid "The provider is delivered by the *Online Bank Sync: Enable Banking (PSD2)* module (``account_bank_sync_enablebanking``), which requires the *Online Bank Sync* module. Enable Banking is a third-party service: you need an account and a registered application with them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:20
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:22
msgid "The people who set up the connection need the :guilabel:`Bank Sync / Manager` access right. The person who enters the private key needs :guilabel:`Bank Sync / Admin` (see :ref:`accounting/bank-sync/access-rights`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:25
msgid "Your database must be served over https, and the *web.base.url* system parameter must hold the address your users type in their browser: Odoo builds the return address of the bank consent from it, and the bank sends your browser back to that address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:28
msgid "Your bank must be one of those offered by Enable Banking for its country. The list is loaded from Enable Banking when you set up the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:30
msgid "Each bank account should have its own :ref:`bank journal <accounting/bank/create>`, or you let Odoo create the journals from the IBANs delivered by the bank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:36
msgid "Register an application at Enable Banking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:38
msgid "This is done on the Enable Banking site (its *Control Panel*), not in Odoo. Create an application with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:41
msgid "**Environment**: :guilabel:`Sandbox` gives you mock banks to try the connection without touching real accounts; :guilabel:`Production` gives you your real banks. The environment is a property of the application, so register one application per environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:44
msgid "**Redirect URL**: ``https://<your database address>/bank_sync/callback/enablebanking``. This is the page where the bank sends you back to Odoo after the consent. It must be identical to the address Odoo uses, including the ``https://`` scheme, otherwise the consent is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:47
msgid "**Key pair**: Odoo signs every request with the private key of the application. Generate the pair on your own computer and upload only the public certificate, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:55
msgid "Alternatively, let the Control Panel generate the pair and download the ``.pem`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:57
msgid "Enable Banking then shows the **application id** of the application. You need this id and the private key file (PEM format) in Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:61
msgid "The private key allows anyone who holds it to access the accounts you connect. Keep the file in a safe place and never send it by email or paste it into a chat, a ticket or a document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:65
msgid "A production application that has no commercial agreement with Enable Banking is, according to Enable Banking's rules at the time of writing, limited to the bank accounts of its owner, which are linked in the Control Panel. Check the conditions with Enable Banking before you connect the accounts of other companies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:73
msgid "Enter the credentials in Odoo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:75
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings` and, in the :guilabel:`Bank & Cash` section, find :guilabel:`Enable Banking (PSD2)`. The setting is stored per company. Fill out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:78
msgid ":guilabel:`Enable Banking environment`: :guilabel:`Sandbox` (default) or :guilabel:`Production`, matching the application you registered. New connections take this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:80
msgid ":guilabel:`Enable Banking application id`: the id shown by the Control Panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:81
msgid ":guilabel:`Enable Banking private key (PEM)`: the whole content of the private key file, from the ``-----BEGIN ... PRIVATE KEY-----`` line to the ``END`` line. The field is only displayed to users of the :guilabel:`Bank Sync / Admin` group: users with the :guilabel:`Bank Sync / Manager` right can use the connection, but cannot read the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:86
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Save`. The description of the setting repeats the redirect URL to register at Enable Banking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:99
msgid "Use a separate application for one connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:101
msgid "A connection can carry its own :guilabel:`Enable Banking application id` and :guilabel:`Enable Banking private key (PEM)` in its :guilabel:`Credentials` section, for example when the accounts belong to a customer who has an Enable Banking application of their own. Leave both fields empty to use the company settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:107
msgid "As soon as a connection has its own application id, it uses its own private key too: it never falls back to the key of the company settings. Fill out both fields, or none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:113
msgid "Connect a bank"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:115
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Bank Sync --> Connections` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:116
msgid "Enter a :guilabel:`Name` and select :guilabel:`Enable Banking (PSD2)` as :guilabel:`Provider`. The :guilabel:`Environment` is filled in from the settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:118
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Test connection`. Odoo signs a request with your key: the message *Enable Banking application ... works.* confirms that the application id and the key are correct. If the environment of the connection differs from the one of the application, the message tells you so; correct the :guilabel:`Environment` of the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:122
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Credentials` section, keep the :guilabel:`Bank country` (two letters, ``ES`` by default) or change it, and set the :guilabel:`Account holder type` of the :guilabel:`Bank consent` section: :guilabel:`Business` if you log in to the online banking of the company, :guilabel:`Personal` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:126
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Load banks`. Odoo reads the banks that Enable Banking offers for the country and the holder type, and confirms it with *N banks available in ES.* Select your bank in the :guilabel:`Bank` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:129
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Connect to bank`. Your browser opens the login page of your bank; identify yourself and authorize the access to your accounts, as you do for any online banking operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:131
msgid "The bank sends you back to Odoo, on the connection. It is now :guilabel:`Connected`, and :guilabel:`Consent valid until` shows the end of the consent. The :guilabel:`Session status` field shows the state of the session at Enable Banking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:146
msgid "The consent lasts as long as the bank allows, at most 180 days. The :guilabel:`Max. consent (days)` column of :menuselection:`Accounting --> Bank Sync --> Banks (Enable Banking)` shows the maximum for each bank; the list is filtered on Spain by default, and the :guilabel:`Holder types` column shows whether the bank offers business and/or personal logins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:152
msgid "In the sandbox, the mock banks of Enable Banking can be listed under another country than yours. If you do not find the mock bank, change the :guilabel:`Bank country` and load the banks again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:156
msgid ":guilabel:`Load banks` only lists the banks for the selected :guilabel:`Account holder type`. After changing the type, load the banks again. Banks that Enable Banking no longer returns for the country are archived in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:163
msgid "The accounts and their journals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:165
msgid "When the consent is completed, Odoo reads the accounts of the bank session and creates one :guilabel:`Bank Sync Account` for each of them, in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Bank Sync --> Accounts`. Each account is linked to a bank journal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:169
msgid "if a bank journal of the company already has a bank account with the **same IBAN**, that journal is used;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:171
msgid "otherwise, Odoo creates a bank journal named after the account, with a code starting with ``EB`` and the IBAN set as its bank account. The journal takes the currency of the account when it differs from the company currency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:175
msgid "A journal linked to an account has its :guilabel:`Bank Feeds` setting switched to :guilabel:`Online Bank Sync`. The :guilabel:`Import (OCA)` button then disappears from the journal card, but statement files can still be imported with the :guilabel:`Import Statement (OCA)` link, for example to :ref:`back-fill the older history <accounting/bank/import-backfill>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:180
msgid "The accounts are created with :guilabel:`Sync enabled` switched **off** and a :guilabel:`Sync every` interval of 6 hours. To start the automatic import, switch :guilabel:`Sync enabled` on for each account, and ask your system administrator to enable the *Online Bank Sync: pull statements* scheduled action (see :ref:`accounting/bank-sync/run`). You can click :guilabel:`Sync now` at any time to get the first transactions immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:187
msgid "Check the :guilabel:`Journal` of every new account. If your bank did not deliver the IBAN, or if the journal's bank account has a different number, Odoo creates a new journal instead of using your existing one. Change the :guilabel:`Journal` of the account, and archive the journal that was created by mistake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:192
msgid "Use :guilabel:`Discover accounts` on the connection to read the accounts of the session again, for example after the bank added an account to the consent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:196
msgid "What is imported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:198
msgid "Odoo asks the bank for the transactions since the last successful run, with a 48-hour overlap, and books the following as bank statement lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:201
msgid "only **booked** transactions. Pending ones are ignored until the bank has booked them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:202
msgid "the amount, negative for a debit and positive for a credit, and the booking date (or, when the bank does not send it, the value date or the transaction date);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:204
msgid "the :guilabel:`Label`, made of the remittance information of the bank (or, in this order, its note, the name of the counterparty or the transaction reference);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:206
msgid "the counterparty name and IBAN, when the bank delivers them, which help to recognize the partner during :doc:`reconciliation <reconciliation>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:208
msgid "a note with the bank's transaction description, reference number and remark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:210
msgid "Every line keeps the transaction id of the bank, prefixed with ``EB-``. When the bank does not send any id, Odoo builds a stable one from the date, the amount, the label and the counterparty. This id is what prevents duplicates: running a synchronization again, or renewing the consent, never books a transaction twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:215
msgid "The first synchronization only reaches back a short time. If you need the history that precedes the connection, import a statement file: :ref:`accounting/bank/import-backfill`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:218
msgid "After the transactions, Odoo reads the balance of the account and runs the :ref:`balance check <accounting/bank-sync/balance-check>`. It uses the booked closing balance of the bank; if the bank does not report one, the interim, expected, opening or available balance is used, in that order. With an available balance the comparison can differ from your books by the amount of the pending operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:225
msgid "Limits of the bank interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:227
msgid "PSD2 allows the bank to limit the automatic calls made while you are not in front of your screen to **4 per account and day**. Odoo respects that limit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:230
msgid "the connection has :guilabel:`Max. unattended syncs per day` set to 4, and the scheduled runs of an account are spread at least 6 hours apart. Once the 4 runs of the day (UTC) are used, the next scheduled run waits for the next day;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:233
msgid ":guilabel:`Sync now` is a run made while you are present. Odoo does not count it, and tells the bank that the request comes from the customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:236
msgid "If the bank refuses a request because the limit was reached anyway, the account shows the message *The bank refused the request: daily access limit reached (PSD2 allows 4 automatic updates a day). Try again tomorrow or sync manually.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:243
msgid "Renew the consent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:245
msgid "The consent ends at :guilabel:`Consent valid until`. Seven days before (or the number of days set in :guilabel:`Remind days before expiry`), the :guilabel:`Consent responsible` receives a :guilabel:`Renew the bank consent` activity. To renew:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:249
msgid "Open the connection and click :guilabel:`Renew consent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:250
msgid "Authorize the access again at your bank, as for the first consent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:251
msgid "Back in Odoo, check that :guilabel:`Consent valid until` moved forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:253
msgid "You can renew at any time, also after the connection has expired. A renewal creates a new session at Enable Banking and closes the previous one. Because a bank can give a new identifier to each account of a new session, Odoo recognizes the accounts again by their stable account identity or, failing that, their IBAN: your journals, the synchronization settings and the imported transactions are kept. Some banks only accept one active consent per customer and application, so a new consent can end the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:260
msgid "To end the access on purpose, click :guilabel:`Disconnect` on the connection and confirm: the session is closed at Enable Banking, the connection goes back to :guilabel:`Draft`, and a new authorization at the bank is needed to connect again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:265
#: ../../content/applications/finance/payment_providers/redsys.rst:206
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/enable_banking.rst:267
msgid "Errors of a scheduled or manual synchronization are shown on the account (:guilabel:`Last state` :guilabel:`Error` and :guilabel:`Last error`); errors of a button on the connection are displayed in a dialog. Keys and tokens are removed from the messages."
msgstr ""

