msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:220
msgid "Importing a file twice"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:222
msgid "Every movement of the file gets an identifier made of the account, the operation and value dates, the concepts, the amount, the document number, the references and the text of the complementary records. Importing the same file again, or two files whose periods overlap (for example the first half of the month, then the whole month), creates each movement only once, and the message *N transactions had already been imported and were ignored.* tells you how many were skipped. Two identical movements of the same file (for example two card payments of the same amount on the same day) are told apart by their order, so both are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:231
msgid "The identifier is built from the whole movement: if a bank sends the same movement again with a different text or reference, it is imported again. Movements imported before this protection existed have no identifier and cannot be recognized: do not re-import a period that you already loaded with an earlier version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:239
msgid "Concept codes on the transactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:241
msgid "Three fields of the Norma 43 movement are kept on the transaction, in its :guilabel:`Technical Information` tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:244
msgid ":guilabel:`N43 common concept`: the two-digit AEB *common concept*, that is the same for all banks (for example 03 for direct debits, 04 for transfers, 12 for cards, 14 for returns and unpaid items, 15 for payrolls, 17 for interest, fees and taxes). The names of the codes are given in Spanish, as in the AEB specification;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:248
msgid ":guilabel:`N43 bank concept`: the three-character code that is specific to the bank;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:249
msgid ":guilabel:`N43 document number`: the document number of the movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:251
msgid "You can search the transactions by :guilabel:`N43 common concept`, for example to find all the bank charges. The fields are read-only and are only filled by the import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:257
msgid "Recognizing the partner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:259
msgid "With :guilabel:`Partner search for N43 import`, Odoo tries to set the partner of every imported transaction from the complementary records of the movement. The counterparty name of the bank is also kept in the transaction whether or not a partner is found. The options are :guilabel:`None` (no search), one bank (:guilabel:`CaixaBank`, :guilabel:`Santander`, :guilabel:`Sabadell`, :guilabel:`BBVA`, :guilabel:`Bankinter`, :guilabel:`Unicaja`, :guilabel:`Kutxabank`, :guilabel:`ING`, :guilabel:`Abanca`, :guilabel:`Ibercaja`), or :guilabel:`All`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:266
msgid "With one bank, only the rule of that bank is used. With :guilabel:`All`, the rules are tried in this order, until a partner is found:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:269
msgid "the rule of the bank that issued the file, recognized by the bank code of the file (the four digits that follow the check digits in a Spanish IBAN; see the table);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:271
msgid "a general search: the tax id (NIF, NIE or CIF, checked for validity) found in the concept texts against the :guilabel:`Tax ID` of your contacts, then a valid IBAN against the bank accounts of your contacts, then the counterparty name;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:274
msgid "the rules of the other banks, in the order of the list above."
msgstr ""

