msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:354
msgid "This check is performed by the *Online Bank Sync: skip synchronized lines on file import* module (``account_bank_sync_statement_import``). It is installed automatically when the *Online Bank Sync* and the *Import Statement Files* modules are both installed. It applies to the generic import dialog and its formats (Norma 43, camt, OFX...), not to the importers of the Hungarian banks, which have their own duplicate check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:361
msgid "How a file line is matched"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:363
msgid "A line of the file is considered as already synchronized when the journal has a synchronized line with the **same amount** and one of the following is true, checked in this order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:366
msgid "the line carries the **bank transaction id** of the synchronized line (in its reference or as a word of its label; a provider prefix such as ``EB-`` is ignored), and the dates are at most 7 days apart, or the tolerance of the journal if it is larger;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:369
msgid "the dates are within the **date tolerance** of the journal, and the labels, references or counterparty names have a word in common;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:371
msgid "the line is the **only** synchronized line with that amount within the date tolerance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:373
msgid "Each synchronized line is used once: if the file holds two identical payments and the synchronization booked one, the second one is imported. Lines already imported from a file are left to the usual duplicate check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:377
msgid "The matching is configured on the bank journal, in the :guilabel:`Bank Account Number` group of the :guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:380
msgid ":guilabel:`Skip lines already synchronized online`: on by default. Switch it off to import every line of the file;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:382
msgid ":guilabel:`Date tolerance (days)`: 2 by default, displayed when the option is on. It is the maximum difference between the date of the line in the file and the date of the synchronized line. Banks often give a different date for the same transaction (value date or booking date, or a weekend in between)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:387
msgid "If every line of the file was skipped, Odoo reports that the file was already imported, and adds the list of the lines recognized as synchronized. The message lists at most 20 lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:391
msgid "The check works in one direction only: a later synchronization does not look at the lines that were imported from a file. Do not import a file for a period that the synchronization has not loaded yet, or the same transactions will be booked twice. Files are meant for the period that precedes the connection, or that the synchronization has already loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:397
msgid "Rule 3 accepts a single synchronized line with the same amount as a match even without any common text. If two different payments of the same amount fall within the tolerance, check the list of skipped lines in the preview and lower the tolerance (0 means the same date) or switch the option off for that import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/statement_import.rst:404
