#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:352
msgid "goods: :guilabel:`VTSZ` (customs tariff number) and :guilabel:`KN` (Combined Nomenclature);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:353
msgid "services: :guilabel:`SZJ`, :guilabel:`TESZOR` and :guilabel:`Intermediated Service by Default` (invoice lines of the product are marked as :ref:`intermediated service <localizations/hungary/intermediated>` automatically)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:357
msgid "The code lists are maintained by administrators in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> VTSZ, KN, SZJ, TESZOR`, under :guilabel:`Vámtarifaszám (VTSZ)` and :guilabel:`Kombinált Nómenklatúra (KN)`. The VTSZ numbers of the goods subject to domestic reverse charge (cereals, oilseeds, steel products) are preloaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:363
msgid "There is no menu for the SZJ and TESZOR lists in the current module version; new codes can be created from the product form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:366
msgid "The NAV report requires a standard unit type for each unit of measure. Open :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Units Of Measure --> Units Of Measure Categories` and check the :guilabel:`NAV volume unit types` column of the units: `PIECE`, `KILOGRAM`, `TON`, `KWH`, `DAY`, `HOUR`, `MINUTE`, `MONTH`, `LITER`, `KILOMETER`, `CUBIC_METER`, `METER`, `LINEAR_METER`, `CARTON`, `PACK` or `OWN` (own unit, reported with its name)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:377
msgid "The following options are available in the :guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab of journals (:menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Journals`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:380
msgid ":guilabel:`Invoice Format` (all journals): :guilabel:`Paper-based` or :guilabel:`Electronic` default :ref:`format <localizations/hungary/invoice-format>` of the invoices of the journal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:382
msgid ":guilabel:`Foreign VAT (Külföldi adószám)` (sales journals): see :ref:`invoicing under a foreign VAT registration <localizations/hungary/foreign-vat>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:384
msgid ":guilabel:`Hungarian Invoicing` (sales journals, when the NAV data reporting is enabled; visible in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` only): see :ref:`journals for invoices issued in another system <localizations/hungary/external-journal>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:391
msgid "MNB exchange rates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:393
msgid "With the `eyssen_currency_rate_live_mnb_community` module, the :guilabel:`Magyar Nemzeti Bank` provider is available for the :ref:`automatic currency rate update <multi-currency/config-rates-auto>` in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings --> Currencies`; it becomes the default provider of newly created companies. The official rates are stored with the date on which MNB published them; on weekends and bank holidays the last published rates are returned, so no new rate is created for those days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:400
msgid "When the provider is selected, the :guilabel:`MNB Range Load` button loads the historical rates of all active currencies: set :guilabel:`Date from` and, optionally, :guilabel:`Date to` (today if empty; the range cannot exceed 366 days) and click :guilabel:`Load`. Rates that already exist for a currency and a date are not overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary.rst:406
msgid "The rate used on a foreign-currency invoice is the rate of the :ref:`fulfillment date <localizations/hungary/fulfillment-date>`, or today's rate if the fulfillment date is in the future. Credit notes and corrective invoices use the rate of the original invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:3
msgid "Accounting tools for Hungary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:5
msgid "Besides the :doc:`tax returns <vat_return>`, the :guilabel:`Magyar könyvelés és ÁNYK adatszolgáltatás` (`eyssen_l10n_hu_accountant`) module gives accountants the following tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:9
msgid "Change the account of a posted invoice line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:11
msgid "The income or expense account of a **posted** invoice or bill line can be corrected without resetting the document to draft (which is not possible for invoices already reported to NAV). Click the signpost icon (:guilabel:`Change Account`) at the end of the invoice line, or on the journal item in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Accounting --> Journal Items`. In the :guilabel:`Change Posted Account` dialog, select the :guilabel:`New Account` (and, if needed, the analytic distribution) and click :guilabel:`Change`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:27
msgid "The dialog is available to users with the :guilabel:`Administrator` accounting access right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:30
msgid "Accounting date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:32
msgid "For Hungarian companies, the suggested accounting date of a document is based on its own date (fulfillment date) rather than on today. When a lock date is set, the accounting date of sales documents falling into the locked period is moved to the first day of the current month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:37
msgid "Inventory revaluation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:39
msgid "With automated inventory valuation, the value of a single inventory valuation layer can be corrected, for example when the purchase price on the receipt was wrong. In :menuselection:`Inventory --> Reporting --> Valuation`, click the pencil icon (:guilabel:`Change Valuation`) of the row and set the :guilabel:`New Unit Value` or the :guilabel:`New Total Value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:44
msgid "If the layer has a journal entry, the entry is reset to draft, its amounts are replaced and it is posted again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:46
msgid "Otherwise, select the :guilabel:`Journal` and the :guilabel:`Counterpart Account`; a *Revaluation of …* journal entry is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:49
msgid "Every change is kept with the old and new values and the user; the :guilabel:`Change History` icon opens it. Products with the *Standard Price* costing method cannot be revalued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:53
msgid "Dashboard balance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/accounting_tools.rst:55
msgid "The bank and cash journal cards of the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard` display the general ledger balance of the journal's default account (*<account code> <account name> egyenleg*), next to the statement balance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:3
msgid "Hungarian fixed assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`eYssen Hungarian Asset Localization` (`eyssen_l10n_hu_asset`) module extends the :doc:`asset management <../../accounting/vendor_bills/assets>` of the Accounting app with the Hungarian practice:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:9
msgid "rate-based linear depreciation according to the Accounting Act (*Szt.*), prorated by days from the activation date, and a :guilabel:`Lump Sum Depreciation` method;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:11
msgid "an informative depreciation board according to the Corporate Tax Act (*Tao.*), kept in parallel and never posted;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:13
msgid "an activation (commissioning) date with a draft activation journal entry;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:14
msgid "a :guilabel:`Dispose Asset` wizard for scrapping, sale and other withdrawals;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:15
msgid "inventory number, responsible employees, inventory location and other record-keeping fields;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:16
msgid "commissioning, increase, decrease and scrapping protocols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:18
msgid "The module adds the :menuselection:`Accounting --> Fixed Assets` menu with the entries :guilabel:`Assets`, :guilabel:`Asset Categories`, :guilabel:`Post Depreciation` (administrators only) and :guilabel:`Asset Analysis`. The standard asset menus remain available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:23
msgid "The Hungarian calculation applies to purchase-type assets whose :guilabel:`Computation Method` is :guilabel:`Lump Sum Depreciation`, or :guilabel:`Linear` with :guilabel:`Time Method Based On` set to :guilabel:`Number of Entries`, a depreciation rate greater than zero and a period length of 1, 3, 6 or 12 months. Every other asset (degressive, ending-date based, or linear with a zero rate) keeps the standard behavior described in :doc:`../../accounting/vendor_bills/assets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:32
msgid "Open :menuselection:`Accounting --> Fixed Assets --> Asset Categories`. In addition to the standard fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:35
msgid ":guilabel:`Depreciation Rate (Accounting Act)`: the yearly depreciation rate, copied to the assets of the category. Enter it as a fraction (`0.2` means 20%, `0.145` means 14.5%);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:37
msgid ":guilabel:`Depreciation Rate (Corporate Tax Act)`: the yearly rate of the tax depreciation board (20% is used if it is empty);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`Computation Method` gains the :guilabel:`Lump Sum Depreciation` option: the whole value is written off in one entry on the activation date (for example, for low-value assets);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:41
msgid ":guilabel:`Acquisition Account`: the construction-in-progress account (*beruházások*, e.g., `161`) credited by the activation entry. It is required to confirm an asset;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:43
msgid ":guilabel:`Disposal Expense Account`: the expense account (e.g., `86…`) that receives the net book value when an asset is disposed of. It is required to dispose of an asset;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:45
msgid ":guilabel:`Disposal Income Account`: informative; the sales revenue itself is booked by the customer invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:59
msgid "On the asset form (:menuselection:`Accounting --> Fixed Assets --> Assets`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:61
msgid ":guilabel:`Activation Date`: the day the asset was put into service. The activation entry and the depreciation board start from this date; it is mandatory to confirm the asset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:63
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Depreciation Information` tab, the field labelled :guilabel:`Degressive Factor` holds the yearly **accounting depreciation rate** of linear assets (copied from the category), and :guilabel:`Depreciation Rate (Corporate Tax Act)` holds the tax rate. The :guilabel:`Number of Depreciations` is computed from the rate and the period length and is read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:67
msgid "The :guilabel:`Special` tab contains the :guilabel:`Inventory Responsible` and the :guilabel:`Asset Responsibles` (employees), the :guilabel:`Inventory Number` (also shown in the name of the asset and searchable), a :guilabel:`QR Code` text, the :guilabel:`Inventory Warehouse`, an informative :guilabel:`Analytic Plan` and :guilabel:`Analytic Account`, the :guilabel:`Consumed Development Reserve` (*fejlesztési tartalék*, informative), and the :guilabel:`Opening Depreciated Amount` for assets taken over from another system with depreciation already booked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:74
msgid "The :guilabel:`TAO Board` tab shows the yearly corporate tax depreciation: :guilabel:`Year`, :guilabel:`Depreciation Date`, :guilabel:`Current Depreciation`, :guilabel:`Cumulative Depreciation` and :guilabel:`Remaining Value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:79
msgid "How the boards are computed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:81
msgid "**Accounting board**: the depreciation lines are dated at the **end** of each period (month, quarter, half-year or year) of the fiscal year. The amount of a full period is (gross value − salvage value) × rate × period length / 12. The first line is prorated by the actual calendar days from the activation date to the end of the period; the last line takes the remainder, so the board always ends at zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:88
msgid "Gross value 1,200,000 HUF, salvage value 200,000 HUF, rate 0.20, yearly periods, activated on 15 April 2026: 143,014 HUF in 2026 (261 of 365 days), 200,000 HUF in each of the next four years, and the remaining 56,986 HUF in 2031."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:92
msgid "**TAO board**: yearly lines at the end of the fiscal year. The first year is prorated on a 360-day (12 × 30) basis from the activation date. The board is recomputed together with the accounting board and is never posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:95
msgid "The :guilabel:`Opening Depreciated Amount` reduces the residual value on both boards; lines that are fully covered by it are not generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:99
msgid "Confirm and depreciate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:101
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm`. For Hungarian assets, a **draft** journal entry *<asset name>: Activation* is created on the journal of the category at the activation date, debiting the asset account and crediting the :guilabel:`Acquisition Account` with the gross value. Review and post it from the :guilabel:`Activation Journal Entry` link. Confirming does not post any depreciation: the due lines are posted by the monthly scheduled action of the asset management or with :menuselection:`Accounting --> Fixed Assets --> Post Depreciation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:108
msgid "Several draft assets can be confirmed at once from the list view with :menuselection:`Action --> Confirm Assets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:112
msgid "Do not enable :guilabel:`Auto-Confirm Assets` on categories that use the Hungarian calculation: assets created from vendor bills have no activation date, so the bill could not be posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:115
msgid "To change the period length of a running asset, use :guilabel:`Modify Depreciation`; the number of depreciations stays computed. The rate itself can only be changed while the asset is in draft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:119
msgid "Dispose of an asset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:121
msgid "The standard :guilabel:`Sell or Dispose` button is hidden on Hungarian assets. Click :guilabel:`Dispose Asset` (available on running and on fully depreciated assets) and fill in the :guilabel:`Disposal Date`, the :guilabel:`Disposal Type` (:guilabel:`Scrapping`, :guilabel:`Sale` or :guilabel:`Other Withdrawal`) and the :guilabel:`Disposal Reason`. The wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:126
msgid "removes the unposted depreciation lines and adds a catch-up line up to the disposal date, with a draft depreciation entry;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:128
msgid "creates the draft entry *<asset name>: Disposal*: accumulated depreciation and :guilabel:`Disposal Expense Account` (net book value) on the debit side, the asset account (gross value) on the credit side;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:131
msgid "closes the asset, fills in the :guilabel:`Disposal` section of the form and shortens the TAO board to the year of the disposal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:134
msgid "Both entries remain in draft for review. In case of a sale, the revenue is invoiced separately with a customer invoice. A disposed asset cannot be reset to draft or confirmed again. The disposal date cannot precede the activation date or the last posted depreciation, and cannot fall into a locked period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:148
msgid "Protocols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:150
msgid "The :guilabel:`Print` menu of the asset form and list contains four PDF protocols: :guilabel:`Commissioning Protocol` (*üzembe helyezési jegyzőkönyv*), :guilabel:`Asset Increase Protocol` (*állománynövekedési jegyzőkönyv*), :guilabel:`Asset Decrease Protocol` (*állománycsökkenési jegyzőkönyv*) and :guilabel:`Scrapping Protocol` (*selejtezési jegyzőkönyv*). The scrapping protocol shows the net value according to both the Accounting Act and the Corporate Tax Act."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:3
msgid "Cashbook integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:5
msgid "`Cashbook <https://cashbook.hu>`_ is an external Hungarian online service that collects the invoices of a business for bookkeeping and cash-flow follow-up. The :guilabel:`Cashbook integráció` (`eyssen_l10n_hu_cashbook`) module transfers the invoices, credit notes and :doc:`pro-forma invoices <proforma>` of the company to Cashbook automatically, as structured data together with the PDF, and re-sends an invoice with its payment data whenever a payment is reconciled with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:12
msgid "This integration is not related to the :doc:`cash register <../../accounting/bank/cash_register>` (*házipénztár*) feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:14
msgid "The module requires `eyssen_l10n_hu` and `eyssen_l10n_hu_proforma`. Its labels are displayed in Hungarian in the current module version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:20
msgid "Request an API key from Cashbook, then go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, section :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás` (the same fields are available in the :guilabel:`CashBook adatszolgáltatás` tab of the company form):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:24
msgid "tick :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`Üzemmód`: :guilabel:`Teszt üzemmód` (test system, the default) or :guilabel:`Éles adatszolgáltatás` (production);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Ne küldjük be a Cashbook-nak a számlákat. KIZÁRÓLAG TESZTELÉSRE!`: suspends the transfer, for testing;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:29
msgid ":guilabel:`Cashbook kulcs`: the API key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:39
msgid "At installation, a to-do activity *Cashbook adatszolgáltatáshoz be kell állítani!* is created on every company. A copied (neutralized) database is switched to test mode with the transfer disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:43
msgid "Enter the API key right after installing the module. In the current module version, confirming a pro-forma invoice and reconciling a payment fail while the key is empty, even if the :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás` option is not ticked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:47
msgid "To exclude a whole journal (for example, a journal of invoices issued in another system), open it in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` and tick :guilabel:`Nem kell átadni a Cashbook-nak!` in the :guilabel:`Hungarian Invoicing` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:52
msgid "Transfer and follow-up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:54
msgid "Posted customer invoices, vendor bills and credit notes, as well as confirmed pro-forma invoices, are queued when they are confirmed; a background job sends them about a minute later and retries every five minutes. The PDF sent is the main attachment of the document, or the printed invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:58
msgid "The :guilabel:`CashBook` tab of the invoice and of the pro-forma invoice shows the :guilabel:`Cashbook státusz`, which is also available as a column in the invoice, credit note and pro-forma lists: *Beküldés folyamatban* (queued), *Beküldve* (sent), *Sikeresen feldolgozva* (processed), or the error reported by Cashbook (for example, unreadable data, missing PDF, unknown tax number, or missing permission for vendor bills). In :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`, the tab contains the buttons :guilabel:`Beküldés a CashBook-ba`, :guilabel:`Azonnali beküldés a CashBook-ba` and :guilabel:`Státusz ellenőrzés` for administrators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:3
msgid "Extended producer responsibility (EPR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`Hungary - Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR / KGYF)` (`l10n_hu_epr`) module implements the Hungarian extended producer responsibility (*kiterjesztett gyártói felelősség*, Government Decree 80/2023. (III. 14.)): it keeps the EPR register of the products placed on the Hungarian market by KF code, prints the invoice clauses, and prepares the quarterly data report (OKIRkapu data package :guilabel:`KG:KGYF-NÉ`) as an XML file validated against the official schema. It can be installed from the Apps menu or by ticking :guilabel:`Hungarian EPR` in the :doc:`eYssen ERP settings <../../../general/eyssen_erp_settings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:13
msgid "The EPR covers packaging, single-use plastic products, electrical and electronic equipment, batteries, vehicles, tyres, office paper, advertising paper, frying oil and fat, textiles and wooden furniture. The fee is collected by the concessionaire MOHU MOL Hulladékgazdálkodási Zrt. The products still subject to the environmental product fee are handled by the :doc:`KVTD module <kvtd>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:19
msgid "The data report is uploaded to OKIRkapu by the user: OKIRkapu has no machine interface, the module generates the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:21
msgid "The fee is not posted by the module. MOHU invoices it quarterly on the basis of the data report; record the MOHU invoice as a vendor bill and link it to the report to compare the amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:25
msgid "How the obligation works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:27
msgid "The **producer** is whoever places a product on the Hungarian market for the first time: the domestic manufacturer, or the importer or EU purchaser at its first domestic sale (80/2023. Korm. r. 16. §). A company buying from a Hungarian supplier and reselling is not liable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:30
msgid "Every separable component of a packaging (bottle, cap, label, film, carton) has its own KF code and fee (11. § (5))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:32
msgid "The producer reports the quantities by KF code quarterly, by the 20th day of the month following the quarter, to the national waste management authority through OKIRkapu (27. §). MOHU invoices the fee on this basis; it is payable within 15 days of receipt (21. § (1))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:35
msgid "Records are kept for at least 5 years and must be traceable item by item (26. §, 28. §)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:38
msgid "KF codes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:40
msgid "The KF code has 8 characters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/epr.rst:46
