msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:69
msgid ":menuselection:`Accounting --> eVAT --> Configuration --> Mapping Rules` handles the exceptions. A rule has :guilabel:`Conditions` (:guilabel:`Taxes`, :guilabel:`Move Types`, :guilabel:`Partner Status`, :guilabel:`Fiscal Positions`, :guilabel:`Product Categories`, :guilabel:`Products`) and a :guilabel:`Result`: the :guilabel:`eVAT Standard Tax Code` and the :guilabel:`Taxpoint Strategy` (:guilabel:`Default`, :guilabel:`Delivery date`, :guilabel:`Accounting date` or :guilabel:`Period end`). The first matching rule wins; if no rule matches, the default code of the tax is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:76
msgid "A document whose tax has neither a rule nor a default code is skipped and reported on the :guilabel:`Validation` tab of the return (code `GEN0001`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:80
msgid "Other tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:82
msgid ":guilabel:`MNB Base Rates`: the central bank base rate series used to compute the self-revision surcharge. The historical rates are preloaded; **add a new row whenever the base rate changes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:84
msgid ":guilabel:`VTSZ Tariff Mapping`: maps the VTSZ prefixes of domestic reverse-charge goods (agricultural products, steel, gas) to the product category and unit of measure required on sheets `07` and `08`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:91
msgid "Prepare and file a return"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:93
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> eVAT --> Declarations` and click :guilabel:`New`. Set the :guilabel:`Period Start`, the :guilabel:`Period End` and the :guilabel:`Frequency` (:guilabel:`Monthly`, :guilabel:`Quarterly` or :guilabel:`Annual`), then follow the steps below. The status bar shows the main steps: :guilabel:`Draft`, :guilabel:`Generated`, :guilabel:`Finished` and :guilabel:`Submitted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:99
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Generate`. The analytics lines are built from the posted entries of the period (taxes due on payment are included by payment date), the summary is computed, the local validation runs and the reverse-charge sheets `07`/`08` are filled in. :guilabel:`Reset to Draft` discards the generated data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:103
msgid "Review the tabs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:105
msgid ":guilabel:`Lines`: the analytics lines with their source document, taxpoint date and partner;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:106
msgid ":guilabel:`Summary`: payable, deductible, reclaimed and transferable tax in thousand HUF. Tick :guilabel:`Lapsed Residual Tax` if the amount carried forward from the previous period can no longer be used;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:109
msgid ":guilabel:`Statements`: the :guilabel:`Return Decision` (:guilabel:`No return`, :guilabel:`Full return` or :guilabel:`Tax account transfer`), the :guilabel:`Refund Entitlement Code` and the procedure indicators of the return. Click :guilabel:`Compute Summary` after changing them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:112
msgid ":guilabel:`Transfer (170)`: the transfer request lines, if the return decision is a tax account transfer;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:114
msgid ":guilabel:`Reverse charge (07/08)`: the domestic reverse-charge sheets, which can be regenerated with :guilabel:`Regenerate 07/08 Sheets`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:116
msgid ":guilabel:`Validation`: the messages of the local check (:guilabel:`Critical`, :guilabel:`Error`, :guilabel:`Warning`, :guilabel:`Info`). Correct the source documents or the tax code mapping, and click :guilabel:`Generate` again after a :guilabel:`Reset to Draft`. :guilabel:`Validate` reruns the check at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:121
msgid "Optionally, click :guilabel:`Export XML` to download the analytics file (`EVAT_<start>_<end>_v<version>.xml`) for review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:123
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Upload to NAV`. The return must be free of local validation errors. The status changes to :guilabel:`Uploading`, and a background job uploads the data about a minute later. If the upload fails, the return goes back to :guilabel:`Generated` and the reason is shown in the :guilabel:`Error Note` of the :guilabel:`NAV` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:127
msgid "NAV processes the upload. A scheduled action checks the status every five minutes (:guilabel:`Received` → :guilabel:`Processing` → :guilabel:`BEVFELD Check` → :guilabel:`Finished`); :guilabel:`Check Status Now` checks it on demand. The messages of NAV are added to the :guilabel:`Validation` tab. If NAV rejects the data, the status becomes :guilabel:`Aborted`: click :guilabel:`Reopen`, correct the problem and upload again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:132
msgid "When the status is :guilabel:`Finished`, every user with the :guilabel:`eVAT Approve` right receives a to-do activity *Submit eVAT declaration to NAV*. The :guilabel:`Submission Deadline` on the :guilabel:`NAV` tab shows until when the processed data is kept by NAV (30 days); after that the upload must be repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:136
msgid "An approver clicks :guilabel:`Submit to NAV`. The dialog lists the high-priority warnings of NAV, which must be acknowledged with :guilabel:`I acknowledge the warnings above`, and reminds that *submitting is the legally binding filing of the VAT return with NAV* and cannot be undone. After the confirmation the status is :guilabel:`Submitted` and the return document received from NAV is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:151
msgid "The taxpoint date of a document is its fulfillment date, unless a mapping rule sets another strategy. It can be overridden on the :guilabel:`eVAT` tab of the invoice (:guilabel:`eVAT Taxpoint Date`). The same tab lists the returns that contain the invoice, and :guilabel:`Query NAV Tax Codes` shows the codes NAV suggests for a posted invoice (for information only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:156
msgid "Vendor bills are identified by their :guilabel:`Bill Reference`; bills without a reference are skipped with a validation message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:160
msgid "Reconcile with the NAV data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:162
msgid "On the :guilabel:`NAV Documents` tab, click :guilabel:`Fetch NAV Documents` to download the invoice data, cash register summaries and customs declarations that NAV holds for the period. The :guilabel:`Reconciliation Summary` and the :guilabel:`NAV Match` badge of the lines show which documents are :guilabel:`Matched` and which are :guilabel:`Missing in Odoo`, for example vendor bills that were not recorded yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:169
msgid "Self-revision and correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:171
msgid "On a :guilabel:`Submitted` return, click :guilabel:`Self-check` (*önellenőrzés*) or :guilabel:`Correction` to create the next version for the same period, then generate, upload and submit it like a base return. The :guilabel:`Changes` tab compares it with the original return (summary differences and added, removed and changed lines)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:176
msgid "For a self-revision, the :guilabel:`Self-check (04)` tab contains the self-revision surcharge (*önellenőrzési pótlék*). Select the :guilabel:`Non-standard Calculation Reason` if one applies, and click :guilabel:`Compute Allowance`: the surcharge is computed from the MNB base rate, from the day after the original deadline, with a 50% increase for a repeated self-revision. If the surcharge was computed on an earlier day than the submission, the submit dialog asks to acknowledge it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:183
msgid "Scheduled actions and limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:185
msgid "Two scheduled actions are created: *eVAT: poll NAV processing status* (every 5 minutes) and *eVAT: remove finished one-shot upload jobs* (hourly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:188
msgid "The following are not supported in the current module version: the sheets for animal disease deferment, bad debt, chassis numbers and new means of transport; attachments to the return; and the automatic handling of lapsed residual tax. There is no PDF print of the return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:3
msgid "Hungarian invoicing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:5
msgid "The `eyssen_l10n_hu` module adapts customer invoices and vendor bills to the Hungarian VAT Act. The features below are available for companies whose fiscal country is Hungary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:11
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:88
msgid "Fulfillment date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:13
msgid "The :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` (*teljesítés időpontja*) is displayed below the :guilabel:`Invoice Date` on customer invoices, vendor bills and credit notes, and the :guilabel:`Accounting Date` is always visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:17
msgid "On customer invoices, the accounting date must be equal to the fulfillment date. If they differ, the red banner *The Accounting Date is not the same as the Fulfillment Date!* is displayed and the invoice cannot be confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:20
msgid "If the fulfillment date is empty when :guilabel:`Confirm` is clicked, a :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` dialog asks whether today can be used: :guilabel:`Yes, use today` or :guilabel:`No, keep editing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:23
msgid "When a sales order with *delivered quantities* products is invoiced, the accounting and fulfillment dates are set to the date of the latest delivery. With the `eyssen_l10n_hu_sale_stock_delivery_date` module, this also works together with the standard *effective date* logic of the Inventory app; the dates of posted invoices are never recomputed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:27
msgid "Corrective invoices and credit notes always inherit the fulfillment date and the accounting date of the original invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:29
msgid "The exchange rate of foreign-currency invoices is the rate of the fulfillment date (today's rate if the fulfillment date is in the future). The printed invoice repeats the VAT summary in HUF and shows the exchange rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:33
msgid "A yellow banner *The invoice is not made out to the company, but to a contact or delivery address!* warns when the selected customer is a child contact of a company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:47
msgid "Checks at confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:49
msgid "A **customer invoice** or credit note can only be confirmed if"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:51
msgid "the customer has a country, ZIP code, city and street;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:52
msgid "a domestic company customer has a valid :ref:`Hungarian tax number <localizations/hungary/contacts>` (when the NAV data reporting is enabled), and an EU company customer has an EU VAT number that is valid in VIES;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:55
msgid "the fulfillment date is set and equals the accounting date;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:56
msgid "payment terms or a due date are set, and the due date is not earlier than the invoice date;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:57
msgid "the invoice date is **today** (the date of issue cannot be backdated or postdated);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:58
msgid "a :guilabel:`Recipient Bank` account is selected;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:59
msgid "every product line has exactly one tax whose rate matches its :ref:`tax group <localizations/hungary/taxes>`, and a VTSZ number if the tax requires it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:61
msgid "a credit note refers to its original invoice (create it from the original invoice)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:63
msgid "A **vendor bill** needs an invoice date, a fulfillment date and a :guilabel:`Bill Reference`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:65
msgid "A sales order of a Hungarian company cannot be confirmed without :guilabel:`Payment Terms`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:68
msgid "Some of these messages are displayed in Hungarian in the current module version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:73
msgid "Continuous fulfillment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:75
msgid "For periodic settlements (*folyamatos teljesítés*, Section 58 of the VAT Act), tick :guilabel:`Continuous Fulfillment` on the draft invoice. The columns :guilabel:`Start of Period` and :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date / End of Period` appear on the invoice lines; the end of the period is mandatory on every product line. The copy icon next to a date copies it to all lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:80
msgid "The :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` of the invoice becomes read-only and is computed from the latest end of period, the invoice date and the due date:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:87
msgid "Situation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:89
msgid "The due date is before the end of the period and the invoice is issued before the due date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:90
msgid "Invoice date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:91
msgid "The due date is before the end of the period and the invoice is issued on or after the due date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:93
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:95
msgid "End of the period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:94
msgid "The due date is the end of the period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:96
msgid "The due date is after the end of the period, by no more than 60 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:98
msgid "The due date is more than 60 days after the end of the period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:99
msgid "End of the period + 60 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:101
msgid "The period (or the fulfillment date of the line) is printed under each invoice line, and the text *Continuous fulfillment* is printed in the header of the invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:107
msgid "Invoices generated by the *Subscriptions* app are **not** marked as continuous fulfillment automatically. The `l10n_hu_subscription` module only stores the billed period on the invoice lines in technical fields that are not displayed; tick :guilabel:`Continuous Fulfillment` and check the line periods on the draft invoice before confirming it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:115
msgid "Aggregate invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:117
msgid "An aggregate invoice (*gyűjtőszámla*) lists several supplies of a period, each with its own fulfillment date. The :guilabel:`Aggregate Invoice` checkbox is available if the customer has an :guilabel:`Aggregate Invoice Aggreement` (:ref:`contact form <localizations/hungary/contacts>`); it cannot be combined with :guilabel:`Continuous Fulfillment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:122
msgid "Every product line needs a :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date / End of Period`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:123
msgid "All line dates must fall into the same calendar month, cannot be in the future, and the start of a period cannot be later than its end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:125
msgid "The :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` of the invoice is the latest line date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:126
msgid "Taxes flagged :guilabel:`Nem készíthető Gyűjtőszámla ezzel az áfa kulccsal` cannot be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:128
msgid "The invoice is reported to NAV in the *aggregate* invoice category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:133
msgid "Intermediated services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:135
msgid "Tick :guilabel:`The invoice includes an intermediated service` (*közvetített szolgáltatás*) to display the :guilabel:`Intermediated Service` checkbox on the lines, then mark the relevant lines. Lines of products with :guilabel:`Intermediated Service by Default` are marked automatically. At least one line must be marked if the invoice-level checkbox is ticked. The text *The invoice includes an intermediated service.* is printed on the invoice and the flag is reported to NAV line by line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:144
msgid "Corrective invoices and credit notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:146
msgid "A posted invoice cannot be modified. It can be **cancelled** with a credit note (*sztornó számla*) or **corrected** with a corrective invoice (*helyesbítő számla*). All three documents share the number sequence of the journal and are reported to NAV as a chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:151
msgid "Credit note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:153
msgid "The :guilabel:`Credit Note` button is available on posted, **unpaid** invoices that have no corrective, advance or final invoice linked to them. The :guilabel:`Credit Method` is either :guilabel:`Full refund` or :guilabel:`Full refund and new draft invoice`; partial refunds are made with corrective invoices. :guilabel:`Payment Term` can be changed in the dialog. The credit note keeps the fulfillment date, the accounting date and the exchange rate of the original invoice. A credit note or a corrective invoice cannot be credited again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:161
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`Automatically post Credit Note` in the Accounting settings to confirm credit notes as soon as they are created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:165
msgid "Corrective invoice"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:167
msgid "On a posted customer invoice, click :guilabel:`Corrective Invoice`. A draft is created with the title *Corrective Invoice*, today as invoice date, the fulfillment and accounting dates of the original invoice, and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:171
msgid "a section *Helyesbített tételek* (corrected items) containing every line of the original invoice with a **negative quantity**, each followed by a note with the original quantity, unit price and discount;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:174
msgid "an empty section *Új tételek* (new items) for lines that were missing from the original invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:176
msgid "On the corrected lines only the :guilabel:`Quantity` and the :guilabel:`Label` can be edited. Enter the quantity **by which** the original line changes: if 10 pieces were invoiced and 5 were delivered, enter `-5`; to invoice 15 instead of 10, enter `5`. The pre-filled quantities reverse the original invoice completely, so delete the lines that need no correction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:189
msgid "When the corrective invoice is confirmed and its total is negative, it is converted into a *Corrective Credit Note* automatically. The printed titles are *Correction Invoice* and *Correction Credit Note*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:193
msgid ":guilabel:`Corrective Invoice to Zero` is available on invoices that are already (partially) paid. It creates a corrective invoice that reverses the original invoice **and** all its previous corrections, while the payments stay reconciled with the original invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:197
msgid "The :guilabel:`Related Invoices` tab links the documents of a chain: :guilabel:`Original Invoice`, :guilabel:`Correction Serial Number`, the list of posted :guilabel:`Corrective Invoice` documents, the :guilabel:`Final Invoice` and the :guilabel:`Down Payment Invoices` (see :doc:`proforma`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:202
msgid "The lock toggle above the invoice lines prevents the label, unit price and discount of the lines from being recomputed when the product or unit changes. It is enabled automatically on corrective invoices and on bills imported from NAV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:207
msgid "Advance and final invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:209
msgid "When the final invoice of a sales order is created with :guilabel:`Create Invoice` --> *Regular invoice*, the option :guilabel:`Előleg levonása a számlázandó összegig` limits the deducted advance to the value of the products being invoiced; the rest of the advance remains on the order and is deducted from a later invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:217
msgid "Paper-based and electronic invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:219
msgid "The :guilabel:`Invoice Format` field (:guilabel:`Other Info` tab) is :guilabel:`Paper-based` or :guilabel:`Electronic`. It defaults to *Electronic* for customers with an :guilabel:`Electronic Invoice Aggreement`, otherwise to the format of the journal. Electronic invoices are titled *E-Invoice* (*E-Credit Note*, …), are reported to NAV as electronic, and are digitally signed when printed; the sentence *The invoice is valid without signature and stamp!* is printed on paper-based invoices only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:227
msgid "Electronic invoices require the *eYssen E-sign* (`eyssen_esign`) module. Selecting :guilabel:`Electronic` on an invoice also records the electronic invoice agreement on the customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:232
msgid "Other invoice features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:234
msgid ":guilabel:`Payment Dates` tab: the installments of the invoice (due date, label, amount). They can be edited on the draft; on a posted invoice, accountants can move a due date with the :guilabel:`Change Payment Date` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:237
msgid ":guilabel:`Custom Fields` (:guilabel:`Other Info` tab): up to three name–value pairs that are printed in the information row of the invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:239
msgid ":guilabel:`Last Seller`: keeps the name of the salesperson even if the user is later removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:240
msgid ":guilabel:`Address for sending an Invoice`: filled in with the *follow-up* address of the customer, when :guilabel:`Customer Addresses` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:242
msgid ":guilabel:`Delete all lines`: removes every line of a draft invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:243
msgid "**Vendor bills**: the link icon on a draft bill line opens the :guilabel:`Change Purchase Order Line Account` dialog, where the line can be linked to a not yet invoiced purchase order line of the vendor, or unlinked with :guilabel:`Clear purchase order line`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:246
msgid "**Lists**: the :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` column, amounts in the document currency and in the company currency, and grouping by :guilabel:`Currency`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:248
msgid "**Sales orders**: :guilabel:`Delivery Deadline` (free text printed on the quotation) and :guilabel:`Bank Account` (the company account printed on the pro-forma and the invoice). The quotation shows net, VAT and gross amounts per line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:251
msgid "**Numbering**: invoice numbers of the hash-secured customer invoice journal cannot be resequenced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:253
msgid "The printed invoice contains the data required by the VAT Act: the tax numbers of both parties (the group VAT number if applicable), the payment method, the invoice, fulfillment and due dates, the VTSZ/KN/SZJ/TESZOR code of the items, net amount, VAT rate, VAT amount and gross amount per line, totals per VAT rate (also in HUF for foreign-currency invoices), and the declaration that the invoicing software complies with Decree 23/2014 (VI. 30.) NGM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:262
msgid "Invoicing under a foreign VAT registration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:264
msgid "A company that is registered for VAT in another country (for example, because of a local warehouse) issues those invoices under its foreign tax number. They belong to the tax jurisdiction of the other country: they are **not reported to NAV** and must be numbered separately from the Hungarian invoices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:269
msgid "Create a :doc:`fiscal position <../../accounting/taxes/fiscal_positions>` for the country with the :guilabel:`Foreign Tax ID` of the company and the taxes of that country."
