#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:211
msgid "E-Factura"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:213
msgid "The standard integration described in this section sends the invoices to the ANAF *SPV* and receives the vendor bills. The :doc:`rules that Romanian companies add to it <romania/e_factura>` (invoices to individuals and Law 88/2026, submission deadline, storno invoices, SPV messages) are provided by the eYssen *Romania - E-Factura Extensions* module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:221
msgid "Connection to the SPV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:223
msgid "Odoo sends the invoices to the ANAF *Spațiul Privat Virtual* (SPV) with the company's own OAuth credentials. In :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings --> Romanian E-Factura`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:226
msgid "Register an application on the ANAF developer portal with the :guilabel:`Callback URL` shown in the settings block, and copy the resulting :guilabel:`Client ID` and :guilabel:`Client Secret` into the corresponding fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:229
msgid "Keep :guilabel:`Use Test Environment` enabled while testing; disable it for production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:230
msgid "Insert the digital signature USB token, click :guilabel:`Generate Token` and log in to ANAF. The :guilabel:`Access Token` and :guilabel:`Refresh Token` and their expiry dates are then filled in automatically; the token is refreshed by a scheduled action before it expires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:243
msgid "Sending invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:245
msgid "Once an invoice is posted, open :guilabel:`Send & Print` and keep the :guilabel:`Send E-Factura to SPV` option enabled: the CIUS-RO XML is generated, attached to the invoice and uploaded to the SPV. The :guilabel:`E-Factura Status` field of the invoice then shows :guilabel:`Sent`; click :guilabel:`Fetch status` on the line of the :guilabel:`E-Factura` tab to retrieve the ANAF answer, which sets the status to :guilabel:`Validated` (a failed document is listed as :guilabel:`Error` in the tab). The validated document can be downloaded with :guilabel:`Download` in the :guilabel:`E-Factura` tab of the invoice, and errors are logged in the chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:253
msgid "With the *Romania - E-Factura Extensions* module, the invoices to individuals are reported as well, the invoices that are late are followed with reminders, and the messages of the SPV are stored: see :doc:`romania/e_factura`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:266
msgid "Receiving vendor bills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:268
msgid "With the *Romania - Synchronize E-Factura* module, select the purchase journal in :guilabel:`Import Vendor Bills in` in the same settings block. The scheduled action :guilabel:`E-Factura: Synchronize with ANAF` then downloads the invoices addressed to the company in the SPV and creates draft vendor bills from them in that journal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:274
msgid "E-Transport"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:276
msgid "The *Romania - E-Transport* module declares the transport of goods to the ANAF e-Transport system directly from the transfer. On a delivery order or receipt, the :guilabel:`eTransport` tab holds the required data: operation type and scope, :guilabel:`Vehicle Number` (and trailers), the start and end location types, border crossing point or customs office where applicable, and the carrier's partner set on the delivery method. Click :guilabel:`Send eTransport` to obtain the :guilabel:`UIT` code (listed in the :guilabel:`eTransport Documents` tab), :guilabel:`Fetch Status` to update the :guilabel:`eTransport Status`, and :guilabel:`Amend eTransport` to send a correction. The UIT is printed on the delivery slip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:294
msgid "CPV codes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania.rst:296
msgid "The *Romania - CPV Code* module adds a :guilabel:`CPV Code` field to the product form (Invoicing tab). Set it on the products sold to public institutions, so that the code is included in the E-Factura lines when required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:3
msgid "Bank statement import"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`Romania - Bank statement import (MT940, CAMT.053, CSV)` (`l10n_ro_account_statement_import`) module extends the :ref:`generic statement import <accounting/bank/import-standard-files>` with the MT940 files of the Romanian banks and with the recognition of the customers and vendors of the Romanian companies in the imported transactions. It reads:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:11
msgid "**MT940** files, with the layout of the transaction details of *Banca Comercială Română* (BCR), *BRD - Groupe Société Générale*, *ING Bank România*, *Banca Transilvania* (BT), *Raiffeisen Bank România* and *UniCredit Bank România*, and of any other bank that uses the SWIFT standard;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:14
msgid "**CAMT.053** files, with the standard camt statement import module;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:15
msgid "**CSV and Excel** files, with a mapping of the columns (*Statement Sheet Mappings*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:18
msgid "The importers have been developed from the public descriptions of the formats, and tested with synthetic statement files. They have **not** been verified with real files of the banks yet. See :ref:`localizations/romania/statement-status`. Use the :ref:`preview <accounting/bank/import-preview>` of the import dialog on the first files of each bank, and compare the balances and the totals with the statement of your bank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:27
msgid ":ref:`Install <general/install>` the module. The Romanian bank journals get a :guilabel:`Romanian statement import` group in the :guilabel:`Advanced Settings` tab (:menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Journals`, bank journals of a company whose fiscal country is Romania):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:38
msgid ":guilabel:`MT940 bank format`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:39
msgid "Layout of the transaction details (field `:86:`) of the MT940 files of the bank: :guilabel:`Automatic (from the BIC / IBAN of the statement)` (the default), one of the six banks, or :guilabel:`Other bank (generic MT940)`. With the automatic mode, the bank is detected from the BIC or from the IBAN of the statement (`RNCB`, `BRDE`, `INGB`, `BTRL`, `RZBR`, `BACX`); select the bank explicitly if the detection fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:44
msgid ":guilabel:`MT940 transaction date`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:45
msgid "Date given to the imported lines: :guilabel:`Booking date` (the default; the value date is used if the bank provides no booking date) or :guilabel:`Value date`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:47
msgid ":guilabel:`Find partners by CUI / IBAN`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:48
msgid "Enabled by default. When the bank does not identify the account of the counterparty, Odoo looks for an IBAN or a Romanian fiscal code in the details of the transaction, and sets the partner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:52
msgid "Set the bank account number (IBAN) of the company on the journal, so that Odoo can find the journal of a file from the account number it contains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:56
msgid "Import a statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:58
msgid "Open the import dialog with :menuselection:`Accounting --> Accounting --> Import Statement`, or from the card of the bank journal on the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`, as described in :ref:`accounting/bank/import-standard-files`, and select the file. Odoo recognizes MT940 files by their content. A file can contain several statements (several accounts or several days); they are all imported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:64
msgid "For each MT940 statement, Odoo creates a bank statement with the opening and closing balance of the file. Each transaction line gets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:67
msgid "the date, according to the :guilabel:`MT940 transaction date` of the journal;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:68
msgid "the label (details of the transaction), the reference of the customer or of the bank, and the amount, with its sign;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:70
msgid "the name and the account number of the counterparty, if the bank provides them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:71
msgid "a unique import identifier, so that importing the same file again is refused and a transaction already imported is never created twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:74
msgid "The files can be encoded in UTF-8 or in Windows-1250 (the Central European encoding of Romanian diacritics)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:78
msgid "An MT940 file for another bank account than the one of the selected journal is refused with an error message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:82
msgid "Recognition of the partner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:84
msgid "On the journals of Romanian companies with :guilabel:`Find partners by CUI / IBAN` enabled, and for all formats (MT940, CAMT.053 and spreadsheets), the partner of a transaction without partner is found as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:88
msgid "The IBANs found in the transaction details (excluding the accounts of the company) are looked up in the bank accounts of the contacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:90
msgid "Otherwise, the Romanian fiscal codes (*CUI* or *CIF*, with or without the `RO` prefix, written as `CUI 23456783`, `CIF`, `Cod fiscal` or `RO23456783`) are looked up in the :guilabel:`Tax ID` of the contacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:94
msgid "The partner is only set if the match is **unambiguous**: when several contacts share the same IBAN or fiscal code, the transaction is left without partner. The partner is then available for the :doc:`reconciliation <../../accounting/bank/reconciliation>` of the line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/bank_statements.rst:99
msgid "CSV and Excel files"
