#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:3
msgid "Localization base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`Romania - Localization Base` (`l10n_ro_base`) module is the foundation of the eYssen Romanian modules. It provides the data and the tools that the other modules share:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:8
msgid "the :ref:`Romanian Localization settings <localizations/romania/base-settings>` of the company;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:9
msgid "the :ref:`CNP <localizations/romania/cnp>` (*Cod Numeric Personal*) of the individuals;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:10
msgid "the :ref:`lookup of the partners in the ANAF register <localizations/romania/anaf-partners>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:11
msgid "the :ref:`checks of duplicate contacts <localizations/romania/duplicates>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:12
msgid "the :ref:`calendar of the Romanian legal holidays <localizations/romania/calendar>` and the working-day calculations;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:14
msgid "the :ref:`Romanian Localization User group <localizations/romania/user-group>`, which shows the Romanian menus to the users who work on a Romanian company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:17
msgid "It is installed automatically with the other Romanian modules. Its features only apply to companies whose **fiscal country** is Romania; set the :guilabel:`Fiscal Country` of the company in the :guilabel:`Taxes` section of :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`. The other companies of the database are not changed (see :doc:`multi_company`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:25
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/saft_d406.rst:124
msgid "Company settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:27
msgid "In :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, the :guilabel:`Romanian Localization` section (displayed for Romanian companies) groups the following settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:36
msgid ":guilabel:`VAT on Payment`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:37
msgid "The company applies the VAT on collection system (*TVA la încasare*, article 282 of the Fiscal Code). The invoices carry the mention *TVA la încasare* (see :ref:`localizations/romania/vat-on-collection`). Optionally fill in :guilabel:`VAT on Payment From` and :guilabel:`VAT on Payment Until` if the system applies only for a period; leave a date empty for no limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:42
msgid ":guilabel:`Share Capital`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:43
msgid "The subscribed and paid-up share capital (*capital social*), printed on the :doc:`invoices <invoicing>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:45
msgid ":guilabel:`ANAF Partner Data`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:46
msgid ":guilabel:`Autocomplete Partners from ANAF` (enabled by default) fills new contacts from their fiscal code. :guilabel:`ANAF Refresh Interval (days)` (7 by default) is the age after which the scheduled action refreshes the ANAF statuses of a contact; set it to 0 to disable the scheduled refresh. See :ref:`localizations/romania/anaf-partners`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:50
msgid ":guilabel:`Duplicate Partners`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:51
msgid "The :guilabel:`Duplicate CUI / Trade Register No.` policy: :guilabel:`No check`, :guilabel:`Warning only` (default) or :guilabel:`Block duplicates`. See :ref:`localizations/romania/duplicates`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:58
msgid "CNP of individuals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:60
msgid "On the form of a contact that is **not** a company, the :guilabel:`CNP` field is displayed next to the :guilabel:`NRC`, for the contacts of Romanian companies. The CNP (*Cod Numeric Personal*) of the buyer is printed on the :doc:`invoices <invoicing>` and identifies the buyer of the individual invoices sent to :doc:`RO e-Factura <e_factura>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:65
msgid "Odoo validates the CNP when you save the contact, if the country of the contact is Romania or is not set: it has 13 digits and does not start with 0; its birth date is valid and not in the future; the county code (digits 8 and 9) is valid; the sequence number (digits 10 to 12) is not `000`; and the control digit is correct. Spaces are removed when you type. A foreign contact is not checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:72
msgid "The CNP is personal data. The field is only visible to the users with the invoicing or the *Contact Creation* access rights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:78
msgid "Contacts and the ANAF register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:80
msgid "Odoo queries the public web service of ANAF for the taxpayers (*PlatitorTvaRest*, version 9). No credentials are needed; the requests are limited to one per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:84
msgid "Autocomplete of new contacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:86
msgid "When you create a contact and type a valid Romanian fiscal code (CUI) as its **name** (or as its **Tax ID**, while the name is still empty), with or without the `RO` prefix, Odoo fills the contact with the official data: the name, the trade register number (:guilabel:`NRC`), the address with the county, the phone number (if there is none), and the Tax ID, which gets the `RO` prefix only if the company is a VAT payer. The contact is created as a company in Romania. If the code is not found, a warning is displayed. Disable the feature with :guilabel:`Autocomplete Partners from ANAF` in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:95
msgid "ANAF statuses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:97
msgid "The :guilabel:`Romania - ANAF` group of the :guilabel:`Invoicing` tab of the contact shows the statuses of the ANAF register:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:106
msgid ":guilabel:`VAT Payer (RO)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:107
msgid "Registered for VAT in Romania."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:108
msgid ":guilabel:`VAT on Payment (RO)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:109
msgid "Registered in the register of the taxpayers who apply the VAT on collection system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:110
msgid ":guilabel:`RO e-Factura Register`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:111
msgid "Registered in the RO e-Factura register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:112
msgid ":guilabel:`Inactive Taxpayer (RO)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:113
msgid "Declared inactive by ANAF. The VAT of the purchases from an inactive taxpayer is not deductible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:115
msgid ":guilabel:`Split VAT (RO)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:116
msgid "Applies the split VAT payment system (*plata defalcată a TVA*), displayed with :doc:`e_factura`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:118
msgid ":guilabel:`Last ANAF Check`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:119
msgid "Date of the last successful lookup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:121
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Update from ANAF` (displayed when the contact has a Tax ID) to refresh the identity data (name, address, Tax ID, NRC) and the statuses of the contact; a notification tells you if the fiscal code was not found. The statuses are stored on the company of the contact and shared with its child contacts. The filters :guilabel:`RO Inactive Taxpayers` and :guilabel:`RO VAT on Payment` of the contact search find the contacts by status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:127
msgid "A scheduled action, :guilabel:`Romania: refresh partner statuses from ANAF`, runs every day for the Romanian companies. It refreshes the **statuses only** (the name and the address are not overwritten) of the contacts used on the invoices, credit notes and vendor bills of the last 90 days, whose last check is at least :guilabel:`ANAF Refresh Interval (days)` old. If ANAF does not answer, the action stops and tries again the next day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:136
msgid "Duplicate contacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:138
msgid "The :guilabel:`Duplicate CUI / Trade Register No.` setting controls what happens when you create a Romanian contact with a Tax ID or a trade register number that another contact already has:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:141
msgid ":guilabel:`No check`: nothing happens;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:142
msgid ":guilabel:`Warning only` (default): a banner on the contact form tells you that a contact with the same trade register number already exists;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:144
msgid ":guilabel:`Block duplicates`: the contact cannot be saved, and an error message names the contact that already uses the fiscal code or the trade register number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:147
msgid "Only contacts without a parent, whose country is Romania (or empty), in a Romanian company, are checked, and they are compared with the contacts of the same company and with the shared contacts. The Hungarian and Spanish contacts are never blocked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:154
msgid "Legal holidays and working days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:156
msgid "Deadlines such as the :ref:`E-Factura submission deadline <localizations/romania/efactura-deadline>` are counted in working days: the days that are neither a weekend day nor a legal holiday. The legal holidays follow article 139 of the Labor Code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:160
msgid "1 and 2 January;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:161
msgid "6 and 7 January (since 2024);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:162
msgid "24 January;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:163
msgid "Orthodox Good Friday, Easter Sunday and Easter Monday;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:164
msgid "1 May and 1 June;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:165
msgid "Orthodox Pentecost (*Rusalii*) Sunday and Monday;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:166
msgid "15 August;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:167
msgid "30 November and 1 December;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:168
msgid "25 and 26 December."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:170
msgid "The moving holidays are calculated from the date of the Orthodox Easter. To add days off decided by the Government, enable the :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` and create the system parameter `l10n_ro_base.extra_holidays` in :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> System Parameters`. Its value is a list of dates in the `YYYY-MM-DD` format, separated by commas, for example `2026-12-24,2026-12-28`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:179
msgid "Romanian menus and the Romanian Localization User group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:181
msgid "All the menus of the Romanian modules (declarations, registers, E-Factura deadlines and messages, assets and stock reports) are restricted to the members of the **Romanian Localization User** group, in addition to their usual access rights. The group is managed automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:185
msgid "the internal users who have access to at least one company whose fiscal country is Romania are added to the group (when the module is installed, and each time the companies or the groups of a user, or the fiscal country of a company, change);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:188
msgid "a user who loses that access is removed from the group, but only if the group was granted automatically. A membership that you granted by hand is never removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:191
msgid "This way, the users who work only on Hungarian or Spanish companies do not see the Romanian menus. To grant or remove the group by hand, edit the user in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:196
msgid "The menus can be refreshed with a delay when the fiscal country of a company changes: reload the page, or log in again, if a menu does not appear or disappear immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:201
msgid ":doc:`e_factura`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/base.rst:202
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:194
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/saft_d406.rst:426
msgid ":doc:`multi_company`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:3
msgid "Cash documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`Romania - Cash Documents (eYssen)` (`l10n_ro_cash`) module adapts the :doc:`cash register <../../accounting/bank/cash_register>` to the Romanian rules. For the cash journals of Romanian companies, the cash vouchers are printed as the official documents of OMFP 2634/2015:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:9
msgid "the **receipt** (*chitanță*, form 14-4-1), given to the customers who pay in cash;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:10
msgid "the **cash collection order** (*dispoziție de încasare*) and the **cash payment order** (*dispoziție de plată*), both on form 14-4-4;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:12
msgid "the **cash register book** (*registru de casă*, form 14-4-7), printed from the cash-book pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:14
msgid "The module also checks the cash operations against the limits of Law 70/2015 on cash payments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:16
msgid "It requires the *eYssen Accountant* and *Cash register* modules, which are installed with it, and only changes the cash journals of companies whose **fiscal country** is Romania."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:22
msgid "Installation in a multi-company database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:24
msgid "The cash register manages **every** cash journal of the database: vouchers, cash-book pages, numbering and locks. When `l10n_ro_cash` installs the cash register as a dependency in a database that already contains companies of other countries, the cash register is **disabled** for the non-Romanian companies that already have journal entries: their cash journals keep working as before, as in standard Odoo. The companies without entries, the new companies and the Romanian companies get the cash register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:31
msgid "The setting is the :guilabel:`Cash Register Disabled` field, displayed on the cash journals (:menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Journals`, :guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab, for users with the *Adviser* access right on the Accounting app). It belongs to the company: it applies to all the cash journals of the company. If the cash register was already installed, or if you install it yourself, it is enabled for all the companies, as before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:38
msgid "While the cash register is disabled for a company, its cash journals have no cash vouchers, no cash-book pages and no separate receipt/disbursement numbering, and the :guilabel:`Separate Receipt/Disbursement Numbering` field is hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:45
msgid "Numbering of the documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:48
msgid "Cash orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:50
msgid "With the :guilabel:`Separate Receipt/Disbursement Numbering` option of the cash journal (see :ref:`cash_register/numbering`), the cash vouchers of a Romanian journal are numbered in the two series of the cash orders instead of `BEF/` and `KIF/`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:54
msgid "`DI/` for the cash receipts (*dispoziții de încasare*), for example `DI/CASH/2026/00001`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:55
msgid "`DP/` for the cash payments (*dispoziții de plată*), for example `DP/CASH/2026/00001`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:57
msgid "A journal that already numbered vouchers in the `BEF/` and `KIF/` series (before the module was installed) keeps them, because the prefix is part of the numbers already issued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:63
msgid "A receipt is issued for the cash collected from a **customer**: a customer payment, or a cash line reconciled with a receivable account. It has its own gap-free series for each cash journal, `CH/<journal code>/<year>/00001`. The series is created automatically with the first receipt. It is displayed in the :guilabel:`Receipt (Chitanță) Sequence` field of the cash journal (:guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab, for users with the *Adviser* access right)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:69
msgid "The receipt number is given when the payment is posted or, at the latest, when the receipt is first printed. It is never changed afterwards. The number of the cash voucher itself (`DI/…` or the plain number of the journal) is also printed on the receipt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:73
msgid "Any other cash collection (for example, the refund of a vendor) is documented by a cash collection order, and any cash payment by a cash payment order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:77
msgid "Printing the documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:79
msgid "The documents are printed in Romanian when the Romanian language is installed in the database, whatever the language of the partner. The amount is written in words (for example *o mie două sute lei și cincizeci bani*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:87
msgid "Document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:88
msgid "How to print it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:89
msgid "Receipt, cash collection order, cash payment order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:90
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Print Cash Document` on the payment (displayed once the payment is posted), or :guilabel:`Print Cash Voucher` on the cash voucher (see :ref:`cash_register/record`). The payment receipt of a cash payment prints the same document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:93
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:116
msgid "Cash register book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:94
msgid "Open a cash-book page and choose :menuselection:`Print --> Cash Report` (see :ref:`cash_register/pages`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:98
msgid "Receipt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:100
msgid "The :guilabel:`RECEIPT` shows the company (unit, tax ID, trade register number, registered office), the receipt number and date, and the payer (:guilabel:`Received from`, tax ID, trade register number, address), the :guilabel:`The sum of` in figures and :guilabel:`In words`, and the reason (:guilabel:`Representing`), for example *Payment of invoice INV/2026/00012 of 2026-09-25*. It is signed by the cashier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:107
msgid "Cash collection and payment orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:109
msgid "The :guilabel:`CASH COLLECTION ORDER` and the :guilabel:`CASH PAYMENT ORDER` show the name and the position of the person, the amount in figures and in words, and the purpose of the collection or of the payment. They have the signature blocks for the head of the unit, the preventive financial control and the financial and accounting department, and the part for the cashier and for the recipient of the money (the identity document of the recipient is to be filled in by hand)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:118
msgid "The :guilabel:`CASH REGISTER BOOK` prints **one page for each day** of the cash-book page: the company, the cash desk and its account, the :guilabel:`Balance carried over from the previous day`, the documents of the day in the order of the vouchers (document number, number of annexes, explanations, receipts and payments), the :guilabel:`Total`, the :guilabel:`Balance at the end of the day`, and the signatures of the cashier and of the financial and accounting department. The documents that are not posted or are cancelled are marked :guilabel:`NOT POSTED` or :guilabel:`CANCELLED`. A page that is not closed is marked :guilabel:`NOT CLOSED - FOR INFORMATION ONLY`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:130
msgid "Cash limits (Law 70/2015)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/cash.rst:132
msgid "Law 70/2015 limits the cash operations between businesses and with individuals, and the cash that a business may keep. Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings` and open the :guilabel:`Romanian Cash Limits (Law 70/2015)` section, displayed for Romanian companies below the bank and cash settings."
msgstr ""

