#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:53
msgid "Prepare the D390"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:55
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Romania (ANAF) --> Declarations --> D390 VIES Statement` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:57
msgid "Choose the :guilabel:`Year` and the :guilabel:`Month`. The D390 is monthly only; the :guilabel:`Deadline` is the 25th of the following month, moved to the next working day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:59
msgid "Choose how the credit notes of earlier months are handled in :guilabel:`Credit Notes of Earlier Periods` (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:61
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Compute`, and review the :guilabel:`Operations` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:62
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d394.rst:114
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Validate`, then :guilabel:`Export XML`, file the statement, and click :guilabel:`Mark as Submitted`, as described in :doc:`declarations`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:66
msgid "How the operations are computed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:68
msgid "The statement is computed from the posted invoices and bills of the month, whose taxes have a D390 operation type. The :guilabel:`Operations` tab has one line per operation type, country, VAT number and partner name, with the :guilabel:`Taxable Base` in whole lei. A line shows the number of documents, and the list icon opens the journal items behind it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:73
msgid "The VAT number of the partner is split into the VIES country prefix and the number (:guilabel:`VAT Number`, without the prefix). The prefix of Greece is `EL`; `XI` (Northern Ireland) is accepted for goods. The United Kingdom is not an EU member state: operations with a British partner are exports or imports, not D390 operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:77
msgid "The VAT number is mandatory for the types `L`, `T`, `P` and `R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:78
msgid "A partner that is not established in another EU member state, or without the mandatory VAT number, is reported with an error message (`D390_PARTNER`) naming the partner and the document. Check the country and the VAT number of the partner, or the tax used on the document. Operations of a partner outside the EU are not included in the statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:82
msgid "Credit notes reduce the base of the partner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:84
msgid "The totals of the statement (:guilabel:`Total L`, :guilabel:`Total T`, ... and the number of operations) are shown below the lines. The statement is not due if there is no operation in the month: the validation shows the error `D390_EMPTY`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:89
msgid "Credit notes of earlier periods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:91
msgid "A credit note issued in a month for an invoice of an earlier month can be reported in two ways. Set the choice in :guilabel:`Credit Notes of Earlier Periods`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:96
msgid ":guilabel:`In the period of the credit note` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:95
msgid "The credit note is reported as a **negative** base in the month in which it is issued. Odoo shows a warning for the lines with a negative base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:100
msgid ":guilabel:`Rectify the original period`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:99
msgid "The credit note is left out of the month and listed in a warning message (`D390_RECTIFY`) that gives the original period. File a **rectificative D390** for that month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:103
msgid "Rectificatives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:105
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Create Rectificative` on an exported or submitted statement to create a new version of the same month. The XML of a rectificative statement contains the **complete corrected list** of operations, not only the differences, so every base must be positive: the validation fails if a line has a base that is zero or negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:111
msgid "Manual lines and call-off stock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:113
msgid "The lines of the :guilabel:`Operations` tab can be edited, and new lines can be added. A line that is added or modified is flagged :guilabel:`Manual` and is kept when the statement is recomputed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:116
msgid "The :guilabel:`Call-off Stock` tab is filled in by hand. It declares the call-off stock arrangements (art. 275¹ of the Fiscal Code): section `A` for the goods transferred to the intended acquirer (:guilabel:`Country`, :guilabel:`VAT Number`, :guilabel:`Acquirer`), and section `B` for the changes (:guilabel:`Reason`: return of the goods, replacement of the acquirer, other). When the acquirer is replaced, give the :guilabel:`New Acquirer Country` and :guilabel:`New Acquirer VAT Number`. The statement can be exported without call-off stock lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:126
msgid "On top of the common checks, the validation of the D390 verifies that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:128
msgid "each partner and operation type appears **once** (no duplicates), and the base is not zero;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:129
msgid "the country is an EU member state accepted by ANAF, and the VAT number is filled in for the types that require it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/d390.rst:131
msgid "the totals agree with the **D300 of the same month** (warning `D390_D300`): type `L` with rows 1 and 2, `P` with rows 3.1 and 4, `A` with rows 5 and 6, and `S` with rows 7.1 and 8. The exempt intra-Community acquisitions (D300 row 29) explain a difference on `A` and `S`."
msgstr ""

