msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:107
msgid "Choose the :guilabel:`Form` and the :guilabel:`Year`. For the half-year report (S1027), the period is the first half-year of the year. The :guilabel:`Deadline` is 150 days after the end of the year (45 days for the half-year report), moved to the next working day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:110
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Classification` tab, enter the :guilabel:`Average Number of Employees` and the number of employees at year end, for the current and the previous year, then click :guilabel:`Compute`. Odoo shows the :guilabel:`Total Assets`, :guilabel:`Net Turnover` and the :guilabel:`Suggested Category`. Confirm the category with :guilabel:`Use Suggested Category`, or select it in :guilabel:`Entity Category` and tick :guilabel:`Category Confirmed`; the form follows the category. Tick :guilabel:`Public Interest Entity` where it applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:116
msgid "Check the :guilabel:`Header` tab: trade register number, CAEN codes, county code, form of ownership, the :guilabel:`Administrator`, the person who prepared the statements (:guilabel:`Prepared by`, :guilabel:`Preparer Quality`), the audit data and the flags. The statements must be :guilabel:`Approved according to the Law` before they are filed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:120
msgid "Review the tabs :guilabel:`F10 Balance Sheet`, :guilabel:`F20 Profit and Loss`, :guilabel:`F30 Informative Data` and :guilabel:`F40 Fixed Assets`. Fill in the manual data and the adjustments (see below), and click :guilabel:`Recompute` to refresh the totals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:123
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Validate`, resolve the errors, then click :guilabel:`Export XML`. The button :guilabel:`Print Summary` prints a summary of the statements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:125
msgid "Complete the filing outside Odoo (see below) and click :guilabel:`Mark as Submitted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:128
msgid "How the amounts are computed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:130
msgid "The account balances are **not computed by this module**. They come from the computation of the Romanian **trial balance** (*Balanța de verificare*) of the accounting registers, the single place where Odoo computes the Romanian account balances. The trial balance, the general ledger, the account sheet, the inventory register, the financial statements, the :doc:`D101 <d101>` and the micro-enterprise tax therefore always show the same figures. Only the **posted** journal entries are included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:143
msgid "F10 balance sheet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:138
msgid "Closing balances of the trial balance at the end of the period. Column 1 is the end of the previous financial year (the beginning of the year) and column 2 the end of the period. The income and expense accounts (classes 6 and 7) are not balance sheet accounts: the result of the year that is not yet closed into account 121 is added to a virtual account 121, and the unclosed results of earlier years to a virtual account 117 (retained earnings). The account class decides, not the type of the account in Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:149
msgid "F20 profit and loss account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:146
msgid "The turnovers of the period of the income and expense accounts (the previous year in column 1). The entries that close the accounts of classes 6 and 7 into account 121 are excluded when :guilabel:`Exclude Result Closing Entries` is ticked (the default), so that the statements are the same before and after the closing of the year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:153
msgid "F40 fixed assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:152
msgid "Opening balance and debit and credit turnovers of the year per group of accounts: gross values, depreciation and impairment adjustments. The column \"of which disposals\" is manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:156
msgid "The trial balance itself carries the unclosed result of earlier years to account 121 in its opening balance, while the statements show it in account 117. This is expected: the totals of equity agree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:161
msgid "Adjustments and manual rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:163
msgid "Each row and column has three values: the :guilabel:`Computed` value, an :guilabel:`Adjustment` that you can type, and the resulting amount (:guilabel:`Col. 1`, :guilabel:`Col. 2`...). Adjustments are kept when the statements are recomputed. Use the :guilabel:`All Rows` button to see and filter all the rows of the statements in one list, and the journal items icon of a row to open the entries behind it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:169
msgid "Four kinds of data need your attention:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:171
msgid "**Accounts to be split by nature.** Some accounts of the official form must be divided between two rows (for example, the debts due within and after one year, the prepaid items and the short and long term parts of 267, 296, 471, 472, 475 and 478). Odoo puts the whole balance in the first row of the official balance import; enter the other part as an **adjustment** in both rows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:175
msgid "**Manual rows.** The rows with the computation :guilabel:`Manual`, mostly in the F30 informative data, hold data that the accounting cannot provide: arrears, research and development, dividends, public ownership data, the \"of which ... affiliated entities\" rows and the long-term debts. Fill them in as adjustments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:179
msgid "**Derived cells.** The F30 chapter I (profit or loss of the unit) is derived from the F20, and the chapter III from the employee numbers of the :guilabel:`Classification` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:181
msgid "**Column \"of which disposals\" of the F40.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:186
msgid "The validation of the statements runs the official rules of the ANAF structure (totals, signs, F10 = F20 result, A+B+C-D-G-H-I = equity, F10 against F40, F20 against F30 for micro-entities) and, besides them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:190
msgid "**Result of the year.** If the result of the F10 (account 121) differs from the net result of the F20, check that the result of the previous year was transferred from 121 to 117 or 129 and that all the closing entries are posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:193
msgid "**Coverage.** A warning lists the accounts with a closing balance (classes 1 to 5) that no row of the balance sheet takes into account (for example, the VAT accounts 4426 and 4427 not settled into 4423 or 4424), and the income and expense accounts that no row of the F20 reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:196
msgid "**Previous year.** The opening balances are compared with the closing balances of the statements already prepared for the previous year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:198
msgid "**Header and classification.** Trade register number, CAEN codes (4 digits), county code, administrator and preparer, fiscal code and CECCAR registration of an authorised preparer, LEI code, auditor, the reason of the S1004, and the match between the form and the confirmed category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:201
msgid "**Period.** Draft journal entries of the period are not included (a warning gives their number), a warning appears if the financial year is not locked (set the lock date in the accounting settings once the statements are final), and the forms require a financial year 2025 or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:208
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Create Rectificative` on an exported or submitted statement to prepare a corrected version. The statements follow the calendar year: for a financial year that differs from the calendar year, use the S1004 and adjust the amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:212
msgid "The following are **not** produced by Odoo: the notes to the financial statements, the statement of changes in equity, the cash flow statement and the reports (management report, auditor report, approval), consolidated statements (S1030), IFRS statements, the forms of banks, insurers and financial investment companies (ASF), and the declaration of inactive entities (S1046)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:220
msgid "XML validation and filing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:222
msgid "The XML is validated against the XSD schemas published by ANAF for the forms (bundled unmodified), and with DUKIntegrator if the :ref:`DUK validator service <localizations/romania/declarations/duk>` is configured (install the validators of the forms `S1002`, `S1003`, `S1004`, `S1005` and `S1027` that you use). The validation is done **without the PDF**: the official PDF of the financial statements contains the mandatory ZIP file of the annexes (notes, reports, approval), which is assembled with the ANAF assistance program and not with Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/financial_statements.rst:230
msgid "Odoo does not send the financial statements to ANAF. The filing package, with its annexes, is prepared and filed outside Odoo (see :ref:`localizations/romania/declarations/filing`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:3
msgid "Fixed assets (Romania)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:5
msgid "The `l10n_ro_asset` module adapts the fixed asset management to the Romanian rules. It adds the classification of the *HG 2139/2004* (the government decision that sets the classification catalog and the useful lives of fixed assets), three Romanian depreciation methods, and two printable documents: the asset sheet and the asset register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:11
msgid "The Romanian rules only apply to **purchase-type** assets (not sales deferrals) of companies whose fiscal country is Romania. The other assets keep the standard depreciation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:15
msgid "Classification catalog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:17
msgid "The catalog is available in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Management --> Fixed Asset Catalog (Romania)`. It is pre-filled with about 25 common codes of the HG 2139/2004, grouped under their chapters. Each code has a :guilabel:`Denomination`, a :guilabel:`Minimum Useful Life (Years)` and a :guilabel:`Maximum Useful Life (Years)`. Accounting managers can add codes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:23
msgid "Set up an asset category"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:25
msgid "On the asset category, the :guilabel:`Romanian Depreciation` group is shown for Romanian companies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:33
msgid ":guilabel:`Romanian Depreciation Method`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:34
msgid ":guilabel:`Linear`, :guilabel:`Degressive` or :guilabel:`Accelerated`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:35
msgid ":guilabel:`Catalog Code`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:36
msgid "Code of the HG 2139/2004. The useful life takes the minimum of the code by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:37
msgid ":guilabel:`Useful Life (Years)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:38
msgid "Duration of the depreciation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`First Year Rate (%)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:40
msgid "For the accelerated method. 50 by default; it must be above 0 and at most 50."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:42
msgid "The same group is available on each asset, with the computed :guilabel:`Degressive Coefficient` and :guilabel:`Annual Depreciation Rate (%)`. The method, the catalog code and the useful life of an asset can only be changed in draft. The :guilabel:`Commissioning Date` is next to the date of the asset; it defaults to the date of the asset, and the depreciation starts the month after. If the useful life is outside the range of the catalog code, a banner warns you that the tax depreciation follows the catalog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:50
msgid "Depreciation methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:52
msgid "The depreciation board has one line per month, dated on the last day of the month. The years of the useful life are counted from the first depreciation month. The last month absorbs the rounding differences, and the salvage value is respected. Posted lines are kept when the board is recomputed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:58
msgid "Linear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:58
msgid "The same amount every year. The annual rate is 100 / useful life."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:64
msgid "Degressive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:61
msgid "The rate is the linear rate times a coefficient, applied to the remaining value: 1.5 for a useful life of 2 to 5 years, 2.0 for 6 to 10 years and 2.5 above 10 years (1.0 for a useful life of one year). When the linear amount of the remaining value becomes higher, the depreciation switches to linear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:68
msgid "Accelerated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:67
msgid "The first year takes the :guilabel:`First Year Rate (%)` (50% at most), and the remainder is linear over the remaining years."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:71
msgid "An asset of 12,000 over 5 years in linear mode gives 60 monthly entries of 200.00, starting at the end of the month after the commissioning. A degressive asset of 10,000 over 5 years depreciates by 3,000, then 2,100, then 1,633.33 for the last three years. An accelerated asset of 12,000 over 4 years gives 12 entries of 500 in the first year, then 166.67 per month."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:77
msgid "Documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:80
msgid "Asset sheet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:82
msgid "On the asset, click :guilabel:`Print Asset Sheet` to print the *Fișa mijlocului fix* (OMFP 2634/2015, form 14-2-2): the data of the asset, the operations, and the depreciation by year (planned and booked)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:87
msgid "Asset register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:89
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Management --> Fixed Asset Register (Romania)`, select the :guilabel:`At Date` and the :guilabel:`Companies`, then click :guilabel:`Print`. The *Registrul mijloacelor fixe* is a landscape PDF with the number, the inventory number, the name, the classification code, the commissioning date, the useful life, the method, the input value, the accumulated depreciation and the net book value of each asset. It lists the purchase-type assets that are running or closed and dated on or before the selected date; the accumulated depreciation is the sum of the posted lines up to that date. The documents are printed in Romanian if the language is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:99
msgid "Differences with other localizations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:101
msgid "The :doc:`Hungarian assets <../hungary/assets>` use a rate-based board per accounting and tax rules (*Szt.* / *Tao*), an activation date, protocols, and a dispose wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:103
msgid "The :doc:`Spanish assets <../spain/fixed_assets>` use three Spanish methods (linear over the useful life, fixed annual percentage and declining balance), with periods that follow the calendar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:106
msgid "The Romanian assets use the catalog codes of the HG 2139/2004 and a monthly engine with a useful life in years."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:110
msgid "Interaction with SAF-T"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:112
msgid "The :doc:`SAF-T D406 <saft_d406>` assets variant reads the catalog code, the useful life and rate, the commissioning date and the SAF-T disposal fields of the asset. Fill the catalog code on each category to avoid a warning at validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/romania/fixed_assets.rst:118
