msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:345
msgid "The community Veri*Factu, Facturae, TicketBAI and Point of Sale modules, and the community Spanish fixed asset module, are refused as long as *Spain - Accounting (PGCE 2008)* is installed. The other alternatives are refused only once the supported module of the pair (*AEAT Base*, *L10n EU OSS OCA* or *Spain - Fixed Assets*) is installed: the standard OSS module, for example, remains available for a Hungarian company that does not use the Spanish OSS. The refusal applies to installations from the Apps menu and from the command line. It shows the message *The Spanish localisation supports one module of each of these pairs only* or the message that Odoo shows for incompatible modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:354
msgid "If an alternative module is already installed, uninstall it before installing the supported one. Ask your system administrator before uninstalling a module, as its data is deleted. If a database already contains both modules of a pair, Odoo does not block other installations, but it writes a warning in the server log when one of them is updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:362
msgid "Promissory notes and confirming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:364
msgid "A vendor bill that is settled with a promissory note (*pagaré*) or a confirming remittance is not paid until the bank debits the amount (Código Civil art. 1170). In Spanish companies, the bill therefore stays :guilabel:`In Payment` while the payment is registered on a payable account, such as the account 401 of the promissory notes or the account 400100 of the confirming, and it is not reconciled with the bank statement line. It becomes :guilabel:`Paid` when you reconcile the bank debit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:371
msgid "The bank step of the :ref:`setup wizard <localizations/spain/setup-wizard>` sets up the payment method and the account of the bank journal for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:375
