msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:386
msgid "You can reach the **Chart of Accounts** by going to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Accounting: Chart of Accounts`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:390
msgid "When a new database is created for a Spanish company, **Spain - SMEs (2008)** is installed by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:396
msgid "Default Spain-specific taxes are created automatically when the :guilabel:`Spanish - Accounting (PGCE 2008) (l10n_es)` module is installed. Each tax is mapped to the boxes of the Spanish **Modelo 303** VAT return, which can be reviewed in the :doc:`tax report <../accounting/reporting/dynamic_reports>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:402
msgid "With the :ref:`Spanish setup <localizations/spain/base-layer>` (fiscal profile), the AEAT tax declarations (modelos 303, 390, 111, 115, 347, 349, and others), the VAT books, and the official PGC annual accounts are prepared in the Accounting app. See :doc:`spain/aeat_declarations`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:409
msgid "VAT regime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:411
msgid "The :guilabel:`VAT regime` of the company is set in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, :guilabel:`Spain` section (or in step :guilabel:`3. Tax regime` of the :ref:`company setup wizard <localizations/spain/setup-wizard>`). Of the available regimes, only the **cash accounting regime (RECC)** changes how the taxes of the invoices are chosen: with it, the domestic VAT of sales and purchases is due on payment. See :doc:`spain/cash_accounting`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:420
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:3
msgid "SII (Suministro Inmediato de Información)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:422
msgid "The *Spain - SII EDI Suministro de Libros* (`l10n_es_edi_sii`) module sends the VAT information of customer invoices and vendor bills to the SII (*Llevanza de libros registro*) of the AEAT or of the regional tax agencies. It is mandatory for companies with a turnover above 6 M€ and optional for the others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:428
msgid "This module cannot be installed together with *AEAT Base* (`l10n_es_aeat`), which the :ref:`fiscal profile <localizations/spain/fiscal-profile>` installs. With the fiscal profile (option :guilabel:`SII Taxpayer`), the SII is handled by the community *Suministro Inmediato de Información en el IVA* module, see :doc:`spain/sii`. Use the module described in this section only on databases without the Spanish AEAT modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:437
msgid ":ref:`Install <general/install>` the :guilabel:`Spain - SII EDI Suministro de Libros (l10n_es_edi_sii)` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:439
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, scroll to the :guilabel:`Registro de Libros connection SII` setting and select the :guilabel:`Tax Agency for SII` (:guilabel:`Agencia Tributaria española`, :guilabel:`Hacienda Foral de Gipuzkoa`, :guilabel:`Hacienda Foral de Bizkaia`, or :guilabel:`Hacienda Foral de Navarra`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:443
msgid "Click the :guilabel:`Certificate (SII)` link to upload the company's digital certificate (file and password) used to sign the requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:445
msgid "Keep :guilabel:`SII Test Mode` enabled while testing; disable it to send the data to the production web service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:447
msgid "On each sales and purchase journal that must report to the SII, enable the :guilabel:`SII IVA Llevanza de libros registro (ES)` format in the :guilabel:`Electronic invoicing` field of the :guilabel:`Advanced Settings` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:462
msgid "The Spanish taxes carry a :guilabel:`Tax Type (Spain)` (:guilabel:`Sujeto`, :guilabel:`Exento`, :guilabel:`Sujeto ISP`, :guilabel:`No Sujeto`, :guilabel:`Retencion`, :guilabel:`Recargo de Equivalencia`, :guilabel:`DUA`, …), an :guilabel:`Exempt Reason (Spain)` for exempt taxes (E1 … E6) and the :guilabel:`Bien de Inversion` flag, which determine how the amounts are reported to the SII. The default taxes are configured; check these fields when creating new taxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:469
msgid "Sending documents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:471
msgid "Once a customer invoice or vendor bill is posted in a journal with the SII format enabled, it is sent to the SII by the scheduled action of the electronic invoicing (or immediately with the :guilabel:`Process now` link of the blue banner). The status is shown in the :guilabel:`Electronic invoicing` field; the CSV return code and the acceptance message (or the errors reported by the agency) are logged in the chatter. The :guilabel:`Registration Date` field of the document (Other Info tab) is the date reported as *fecha de registro contable* for vendor bills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:485
msgid "The Veri*Factu invoicing system used by eYssen is declared to the AEAT by its producer, which issues the *declaración responsable* (responsible declaration) of each release. The declaration is available inside the application, see :ref:`localizations/spain/veri-factu-declaration`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:489
msgid "**Veri*Factu** is an e-Invoicing system used by the Spanish Tax Agency. It is mandatory for most taxpayers in Spain, except for those who use the SII system or are under a regional tax regime (i.e., TicketBai)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:493
msgid "Odoo allows :ref:`invoices <localizations/spain/veri-factu-invoices>` and Point of Sale :ref:`orders <localizations/spain/veri-factu-orders>` to be automatically sent to the tax authorities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:499
msgid "Registration with the AEAT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:501
msgid "There is **no registration** of the company or of the software with the :abbr:`AEAT (Agencia Estatal de Administración Tributaria)` to start using Veri*Factu. What you need before the :ref:`configuration <localizations/spain/veri-factu-configuration>` is a **qualified electronic certificate** that the software uses to authenticate itself to the AEAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:506
msgid "**No census declaration.** It is not necessary to report in the *modelo 036* that the billing records are sent with a Veri*Factu system. The option is made tacitly, by systematically starting to send the billing records to the AEAT. A company can join Veri*Factu whenever it wishes, and stays in this mode at least until the end of the calendar year of the first submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:510
msgid "**No registration of the software.** The AEAT does not keep a register of invoicing software. The producer of the software issues the :ref:`responsible declaration <localizations/spain/veri-factu-declaration>` of each version, and you keep the declarations of the versions you replace or update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:514
msgid "**A qualified certificate is always needed**, also to test the system. It can be the certificate of the taxpayer, or the certificate of a representative, attorney or social collaborator (for example, a tax advisory firm) who sends the records on the taxpayer's behalf."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:519
msgid "The invoices issued with a Veri*Factu system are real invoices, and their records are sent to the AEAT, also when they are issued only to try the system. Use the :ref:`test environment <localizations/spain/veri-factu-configuration>` for tests: the AEAT requires that the invoices issued by mistake in production mode are :ref:`cancelled <localizations/spain/veri-factu-cancellation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:528
msgid "The Spanish invoicing systems must comply with the regulation (Royal Decree 1007/2023) before **1 January 2027** for the taxpayers of the Corporate Income Tax (for example, an *S.L.* or an *S.A.*), and before **1 July 2027** for the other businesses and professionals (Royal Decree-law 15/2025). Starting earlier is possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:534
msgid "Obtaining the certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:536
msgid "The certificates are issued by the certification authorities recognized by the AEAT. The most common one is the **FNMT-RCM** (*Fábrica Nacional de Moneda y Timbre*), described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:539
msgid "**Self-employed person (natural person)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:541
msgid "Request the certificate online on the website of the FNMT. At the end of the request you receive a **request code**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:543
msgid "Accredit your identity in person in a registration office, with the request code and your original DNI, NIE or Spanish passport. The offices of the AEAT and of the Social Security require an appointment; the offices of Correos do not. Some issuers accept an online request with an electronic DNI instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:547
msgid "About an hour after the accreditation, download and install the certificate from the same website. Make a backup copy of the certificate file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:550
msgid "**Company (legal entity)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:552
msgid "A company needs the *Certificado de Representante de Persona Jurídica* (certificate of representative of a legal entity), issued by the FNMT for entities whose NIF starts with A, B, C or D. It is requested by the legal or voluntary representative of the company, who accredits identity and representation either in person in a registration office, or online in the :guilabel:`Electronic Office` of the AEAT (procedure *ZZ38 - Solicitud Certificados Electrónicos de Representante*). For the online accreditation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:559
msgid "Request the certificate on the website of the FNMT and note the **request code**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:560
msgid "Sign in to the Electronic Office of the AEAT with a personal certificate, and open the procedure :guilabel:`Certificados electrónicos de representante persona jurídica`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:562
msgid "Fill in the data of the represented company and of the representative, and enter the request code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:0
msgid "Form of the AEAT procedure ZZ382 with the represented entity, the representative and the request code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:567
msgid "The AEAT form for the presentation of the documents of the certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:569
msgid "Attach the required documents. The AEAT asks for a recent (15 days) certificate of the *Registro Mercantil* about the company, and one of these two: a recent certificate of the *Registro Mercantil* about the appointment of the representative, or, for a voluntary representative, a notarial power of attorney with a special clause for obtaining the certificate. Joint administrators (*administradores mancomunados*) also provide the application form signed by all of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:0
msgid "Notice of the AEAT listing the documents to present"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:579
msgid "The documents required by the AEAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:581
msgid "Add the files, click :guilabel:`Presentar` (submit), and download the receipt. Then continue with the download of the certificate on the website of the FNMT, as above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:0
msgid "Section of the AEAT form to attach the documents, with the Presentar button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:587
msgid "Attaching the documents and submitting them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:589
msgid "Once you have the certificate file (and its password), :ref:`upload it in eYssen <localizations/spain/veri-factu-configuration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:593
msgid "Representation and social collaboration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:595
msgid "If a tax advisory firm or another third party sends the records for you, the taxpayer must give them the power to do so, through **representation** (*apoderamiento*) or **social collaboration** (*colaboración social*). The AEAT provides specific Veri*Factu authorization models in the section *Modelos de autorización de trámites para colaboradores sociales* of its Electronic Office. The certificate uploaded in eYssen is then the qualified certificate of the representative, attorney or social collaborator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:603
msgid "The records sent in the same batch must belong to the same taxpayer. In a database with several Spanish companies, eYssen sends the records of each company separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:607
msgid "Source of this section: Agencia Tributaria, `Veri*Factu FAQ <https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/Sede/iva/sistemas-informaticos-facturacion-verifactu/preguntas-frecuentes/sistemas-verifactu.html>`_ (page updated 22 July 2026), `declaración responsable FAQ <https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/Sede/iva/sistemas-informaticos-facturacion-verifactu/preguntas-frecuentes/certificacion-sistemas-informaticos-declaracion-responsable.html>`_ (22 July 2026) and `Acreditación de persona jurídica <https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/Sede/ayuda/consultas-informaticas/firma-digital-sistema-clave-pin-tecnica/acreditarse-obtener-certificado-electronico/acreditacion-persona-juridica.html>`_ (8 January 2025, the source of the screenshots), and the `FNMT <https://www.sede.fnmt.gob.es/certificados/persona-fisica/obtener-certificado-software>`_ certificate guide. Reproduced under the reuse conditions of the AEAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:622
msgid "To enable **Veri\\*Factu**, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:624
msgid "Open the Settings app to make sure your company's :guilabel:`Country` and :guilabel:`Tax ID` are correctly set in the :ref:`Companies <general/companies/company>` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:626
msgid ":ref:`Install <general/install>` the :guilabel:`Spain - Veri*Factu (l10n_es_edi_verifactu)` module, if it is not installed yet (the :ref:`fiscal profile <localizations/spain/fiscal-profile>` installs it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:629
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, scroll to the :guilabel:`Veri\\*Factu` section, check the :guilabel:`Enable Veri*Factu` option, and click :icon:`oi-arrow-right` :guilabel:`Manage certificates` to add a certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:632
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Certificates for Veri\\*Factu` list view, click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:633
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Upload your file`, then select a certificate file and enter the :guilabel:`Password` needed to open the certificate (if there is one)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:637
msgid "At least one certificate has to be uploaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:638
msgid "By default Veri*Factu is in testing mode. The data is sent to test servers and is not considered official. When official data can be sent to the production servers, go to the :guilabel:`Veri\\*Factu` section in the :guilabel:`Settings` and disable :guilabel:`Test Environment`. This is only possible when the :ref:`production conditions <localizations/spain/veri-factu-production>` are met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:643
msgid "SII taxpayers are exempt from Veri*Factu: do not use both on the same company. With the :ref:`Spanish setup <localizations/spain/base-layer>` and the community SII module, enabling both is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:652
msgid "Once an :doc:`invoice <../../finance/accounting/customer_invoices>` is confirmed, it can be :ref:`sent <accounting/invoice/sending>`. In the :guilabel:`Send` window, the Veri*Factu option is available if Veri*Factu has been enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:656
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Send` to generate a JSON file containing the invoice details. This file is stored as a Veri*Factu document. In the :guilabel:`Veri*Factu` tab, all corresponding documents are listed by their creation date and current status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:660
msgid "The tab shows two statuses, :guilabel:`Test registry` and :guilabel:`Production registry`. Each document is marked :guilabel:`Test` or :guilabel:`Production`. A record accepted in the test registry is not registered in the production registry. After you disable :guilabel:`Test Environment`, send the same posted invoice again: the new record goes to the production registry and the test record stays. If the registry currently selected on the company has already accepted the invoice, :guilabel:`Send` skips it and does not create a second record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:668
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:706
msgid "To download a JSON file, click on its document in the :guilabel:`Veri*Factu` tab. Then, in the :guilabel:`Open: Veri*Factu Documents` window, click the link in the :guilabel:`JSON` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:672
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:710
msgid "The document should be sent to the :abbr:`AEAT (Agencia Estatal de Administración Tributaria)` immediately. However, it may be delayed due to mandatory waiting periods between submissions required by the :abbr:`AEAT (Agencia Estatal de Administración Tributaria)`. In such cases, the document is automatically sent the next time a scheduled action runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:676
msgid "A Veri\\*Factu **QR code** appears on the invoice PDF. It points to the verification page of the registry selected on the company. Scan this code to verify that the invoice has been received and recognized by the :abbr:`AEAT (Agencia Estatal de Administración Tributaria)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:683
msgid "Cancellation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:685
msgid "The cancellation button is on the :guilabel:`Veri*Factu` tab of the invoice, not in the form header. It is :guilabel:`Request Veri*Factu Cancellation`. A warning is shown above the button, and a confirmation question is asked before the record is sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:689
msgid "The cancellation is sent to the AEAT registry currently selected on the company. If the AEAT accepts it, the invoice is cancelled in Odoo as well, and the same invoice number cannot be submitted again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:696
msgid "Point of sale orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:698
msgid "Once an order has been :ref:`paid <pos/sell>`, a JSON file containing the order details is generated. This file is stored as a Veri*Factu document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:701
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Point of Sale --> Orders --> Orders`. In the :guilabel:`Orders` list view, select the relevant order. In the :guilabel:`Veri*Factu` tab, all the corresponding documents are listed by their creation date and current status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:715
msgid "If an invoice is generated for an order during the payment process, the Veri*Factu document is :ref:`created and sent for the invoice <localizations/spain/veri-factu-invoices>` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:719
msgid "A Veri\\*Factu **QR code** appears on the order receipt, even if an invoice is created for the order. Scan this code to verify that the invoice has been received and recognized by the :abbr:`AEAT (Agencia Estatal de Administración Tributaria)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:726
msgid "Software producer and responsible declaration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain.rst:728
