msgid ":guilabel:`Regularization entries`: the :guilabel:`AEAT Journal` (a miscellaneous journal) in which the regularization entries are posted, the :guilabel:`VAT Counterpart Account` (by default 4750) for the VAT declarations whose counterpart is not computed by the declaration itself, such as the modelo 369, and the :guilabel:`Withholding Counterpart Account` (by default 4751) for the withholding declarations (111, 115, 123 and 216). The modelo 303 chooses 4750 or 4700 from its result by itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:115
msgid ":guilabel:`Submitter and frequency`: the :guilabel:`AEAT Contact Name`, :guilabel:`AEAT Contact Phone` and :guilabel:`AEAT Contact Email` printed in the declarations, and the :guilabel:`Filing Frequency` (:guilabel:`Quarterly` or :guilabel:`Monthly`). If the contact name is empty, the contact data of the current user is used. Monthly filing applies to large companies and to taxpayers registered in the REDEME or in the SII. A new declaration proposes the last closed period of this frequency; annual declarations propose the previous year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:122
msgid "When the *AEAT Base* module is installed, or when a Spanish chart of accounts is loaded, the empty defaults of the company are filled in: the journal named *AEAT declarations* (code ``AEAT``, created if the company has none) and the first accounts starting with 4750 and 4751."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:127
msgid "Only the declarations that create a regularization entry use these accounts and the journal: the modelos 303, 369 and 202. The modelo 202 proposes its own accounts (4752 and 473), see :ref:`localizations/spain/aeat/mod202`. The other declarations only propose the period and the contact data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:143
msgid "Tax map check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:145
msgid "Each declaration adds up the amounts of the taxes listed in its *tax map*: a tax that is in no map line of an installed declaration is silently left out of the declarations. The :guilabel:`Tax map check` setting shows how many active sales and purchase taxes of the company are in this situation. Click the link to open the list of these taxes, or go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> AEAT --> Taxes missing from the AEAT declarations`. In the tax list, the :guilabel:`Missing from AEAT declarations` filter gives the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:152
msgid "Review the listed taxes: either the tax is not used, or it must be replaced by one of the default Spanish taxes. A tax that you created by hand can be mapped by setting its :guilabel:`Equivalent Tax (for AEAT mapping purposes)` to the default Spanish tax it corresponds to. The withholding taxes of declarations that are not installed (for example 123, 216 and 296 for a self-employed person) also appear in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:159
msgid "The tax maps themselves can be consulted under :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> AEAT --> Tax mapping`. Do not modify them unless your tax adviser asks for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:165
msgid "File a declaration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:167
msgid "The declarations are under :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> AEAT`, one menu per declaration, for example :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> AEAT --> AEAT 303 model`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:170
msgid "Click :guilabel:`New`. The :guilabel:`Year` and the :guilabel:`Period Type` of the last closed period, the contact data, and, for the declarations that create an entry, the journal and the counterpart account, are proposed from the :ref:`settings <localizations/spain/aeat/configuration>`. Change them if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:174
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Statement Type`: :guilabel:`Normal`, or :guilabel:`Complementary` or :guilabel:`Substitutive` to correct a declaration already filed. For the last two, enter the :guilabel:`Previous declaration number`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:177
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Calculate`. The boxes of the declaration are computed from the posted journal items of the period. Open the :guilabel:`Tax lines` tab, and use the button at the end of a line to see the journal items that make up the amount of a box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:180
msgid "Fill in the boxes that are not computed automatically, if any, then click :guilabel:`Recalculate` if you changed accounting data in the meantime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:182
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm` when the amounts are correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:183
msgid "For the declarations that create a regularization entry (the modelos 303, 369 and 202), click :guilabel:`Create move` to post it: it moves the balances of the tax accounts to the counterpart account. Use :guilabel:`Show move` to open it. The other declarations have no entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:186
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Export to BOE`, then :guilabel:`Export` in the dialog, and download the file to upload it in the AEAT electronic office."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:198
msgid "The regularization entry is dated on the last day of the period. If this date is in a locked period, a warning banner is shown on the declaration as soon as it is opened (while it is not posted). The :guilabel:`Global Lock Date` and the :guilabel:`Hard Lock Date` prevent the entry from being created: :guilabel:`Create move` shows an error. The :guilabel:`Tax Return Lock Date` only shows the warning. Create the declaration entry before locking the period, or ask an adviser to move the lock date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:206
msgid "A banner also warns when active taxes used in the period are not in any AEAT tax map, as they are left out of the declaration. Click :guilabel:`Show taxes` to list them, and see :ref:`localizations/spain/aeat/tax-map`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:211
msgid "The files of the self-assessment returns (modelos 303, 390, 111, 115, 123, 130, 202 and 216) declare, in the field of the software developer of the AEAT file design, the software producer of the fork. It is the same producer as the one declared for Veri*Factu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:216
msgid "Specific declarations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:219
msgid "The :guilabel:`Result Type` shows whether the result is to be paid, returned, or compensated in later periods. The amount to compensate from previous periods is proposed from the previous declarations. In the last period of the year (4T or month 12), indicate whether the company is exempt from the modelo 390, and if so, fill in the additional data of the activities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:224
msgid "For a company under the :ref:`cash accounting regime <localizations/spain/cash-accounting>`, the operations are reported in the boxes of their ordinary tax when they accrue: on collection or payment, and at the latest on 31 December of the following year. Boxes [62] and [63] (sales) and [74] and [75] (purchases) also report, for information, the base and the VAT of these operations when they would have accrued under the general rule, that is on the invoice date. These four boxes are not part of the result of the declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:232
msgid "The annual summary is computed for the whole year. Fill in the fields that are not computed automatically before confirming it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:235
msgid "Under the :ref:`cash accounting regime <localizations/spain/cash-accounting>`, the VAT accrued in the year, including the accruals on 31 December of the following year, is reported in boxes [643] to [648] (base and VAT at 4 %, 10 % and 21 %) and no longer in boxes [01] to [06]. The total VAT of box [34] includes their VAT amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:246
msgid "Modelos 111 and 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:241
msgid "The withholdings are computed from the withholding taxes of the vendor bills. In the modelo 111, fill in the boxes that Odoo cannot compute, such as the work income paid outside Odoo. The in-kind withholdings of professional activities, such as *7% Withholding income tax in cash* and *15% Withholding income tax in cash*, are reported in boxes [11] and [12]. The annual summaries are the modelos 190 (for the 111) and 180 (for the 115, see :ref:`localizations/spain/aeat/mod180`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:249
msgid "After :guilabel:`Calculate`, the :guilabel:`Partner records` tab lists the partners whose operations exceed the threshold; a record shown in red misses data needed for the declaration. Click :guilabel:`Send emails` to send each partner its record for verification, and use :guilabel:`Confirm as valid` when a partner agrees. Real estate rentals not declared in the modelo 115 can be added in the :guilabel:`Real Estate records` tab. To exclude a contact from the declaration regardless of its amounts, tick :guilabel:`Not included in 347 report` on the contact form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:257
msgid "Under the :ref:`cash accounting regime <localizations/spain/cash-accounting>`, the operations of a partner with VAT due on payment (a company under the regime, or a supplier flagged as under the regime) are marked in the record: in the :guilabel:`Partner info` tab of the partner record, :guilabel:`Cash Basis Operation` is ticked and :guilabel:`Cash basis amount` shows the amount accrued in the year under the regime. These are the positions 281 and 284 to 299 of the file. The entries that accrue the VAT do not repeat the invoices in the annual amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:265
msgid "The :guilabel:`Partner records` and :guilabel:`Refunds from other periods` tabs list the intra-community operations of the period. Delete the operations that must not be declared from these tabs before confirming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:270
msgid "The OSS return is computed from the OSS taxes of the distance sales to consumers of other EU countries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:275
msgid "Modelos 123, 216 and 296"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:274
msgid "Like the modelos 111 and 115, they are computed from the withholding taxes of the vendor bills. The modelo 296 is the annual summary of the 216."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:278
msgid "Modelos 180, 193 and 202"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:278
msgid "See :ref:`localizations/spain/aeat/annual-summaries`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:283
msgid "Annual summaries and company returns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:288
msgid "Modelo 180: annual summary of rent withholdings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:290
msgid "The modelo 180 is the informative return that summarizes, for the year, the withholdings on urban property rents that you declared in the modelo 115: it lists each landlord and each rented property with the base and the withholding. It has no amount to pay or to return, and it creates no accounting entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:295
msgid "**Before you start**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:297
msgid "The landlords are contacts with a VAT number and a ZIP code: the first two digits of the ZIP code give the province of the recipient in the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:299
msgid "The rented properties are recorded under :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> AEAT --> Real Estates` with the cadastral reference, the address, the city and the ZIP code. This menu and the :guilabel:`Real Estate` field of the invoice lines are shown to the users of the *Use AEAT Real Estates* group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:303
msgid "Each rent line of the vendor bills uses one of the leases withholding taxes (*19% Withholding (leases)*, *19.5% Withholding (leases)*, *20% Withholding (leases)* or *21% Withholding (leases)*) and has its property in the :guilabel:`Real Estate` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:307
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:374
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:456
msgid "**Prepare the declaration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:309
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> AEAT --> AEAT 180 model`, click :guilabel:`New` and select the :guilabel:`Year`. The contact data are proposed as for any other declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:312
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Calculate`. The result section shows the number of recipients ([01]), the base and the withholdings of the year ([02] and [03]), and the sign of the amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:314
msgid "Open the recipient records tab (:guilabel:`Registro de perceptores`): there is one record per landlord, property and withholding rate, with the base, the withholding, the percentage and the accrual year. Click the magnifier of a record to see the journal items of its base. You can correct a record in its form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:318
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm`, then :guilabel:`Export to BOE` to get the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:321
msgid "Some labels of this declaration are displayed in Spanish, for example the boxes :guilabel:`Base retenciones e ingresos a cuenta` and :guilabel:`Retenciones e ingresos a cuenta`, and the tabs :guilabel:`Líneas de impuestos` and :guilabel:`Registro de perceptores`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:326
msgid "The number of recipients [01] is the number of records: a landlord with two properties, or with two withholding rates, counts twice. It is also the number of recipient records of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:329
msgid "A line without a property is included in the boxes [02] and [03], but it produces no recipient record: fill in the :guilabel:`Real Estate` field of every rent line before calculating, otherwise the records do not add up to the boxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:332
msgid ":guilabel:`Calculate` and :guilabel:`Recalculate` delete and recreate all the records: do the corrections after the last calculation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:334
msgid "The declaration is an informative return: it is confirmed without a bank account or a result type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:337
msgid "**The BOE file.** It contains one declarant record and one recipient record per line of the recipient records tab, all of 500 positions and ending with a line break. The recipient identification comes from the contact (VAT number, name, and the province from the ZIP code) and the property data from the real estate record (cadastral reference, address, municipality and ZIP code, from which the province is taken). A blank province or municipality means that the ZIP code or the city is missing on the contact or on the property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:347
msgid "Modelo 193: annual summary of investment income withholdings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:349
msgid "The modelo 193 is the annual informative return of the withholdings on investment income that a company paid to its partners or lenders: dividends, interest of loans and other income. It is computed from the same withholding taxes as the quarterly modelo 123, so that its total can be compared with the 123 returns of the year. It creates no accounting entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:358
