#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:482
msgid ":guilabel:`[30] Instalments of previous periods`: the instalments of the same tax period of the 202 declarations of this modality that are confirmed or posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:485
msgid "All the other adjustments (other adjustments [07] and [08], 30 % of the depreciation [37], capitalization and levelling reserves, offset of negative tax bases [14], bonuses [27] and the others) are entered by hand. :guilabel:`[17] Percentage` is proposed from the tax rate: 5/7 of the rate rounded down, or 19/20 of the rate rounded up when the turnover is at least 10 million euros (17 % and 24 % for a rate of 25 %). If the entity applies several tax rates, tick :guilabel:`Several tax rates`: the instalment is then entered per rate. :guilabel:`[33] Minimum payment` is only shown for a turnover of at least 10 million euros and is entered by hand. :guilabel:`[34] To pay` is the result [32] or the minimum payment if it is higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:502
msgid "**Confirm and pay**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:504
msgid "Check the :guilabel:`Declaration type`, proposed from the result: :guilabel:`Nil` when there is nothing to pay, :guilabel:`Direct debit` when a bank account is set, :guilabel:`Payment` otherwise. You can change it while the declaration is not confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:507
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm`. A complementary declaration needs the result of the previous declaration ([02] or [31])."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:509
msgid "When there is an amount to pay, click :guilabel:`Create move`: the instalment entry debits the :guilabel:`Payments on account account` (473 by default) and credits the :guilabel:`Counterpart account` (4752 by default), in the :guilabel:`Journal` of the declaration, dated on the last day of the period. Fill in the three fields if they are empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:513
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Export to BOE`. The file follows the record design DR202 in force from 2025 (version 1.3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:517
msgid "Have the following checked by your tax adviser before filing: the proposed percentage [17], the minimum payment [33] and the formula of the result [32] are not verified for every case. The additional information of the declaration (debt waivers, Canary Islands investment reserve, special economic zone, and similar) is exported with zeros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:527
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> AEAT --> Libros del IVA y del IRPF` and create a book for the period, then click :guilabel:`Calculate`. The :guilabel:`Issued Invoices` and :guilabel:`Received Invoices` tabs list the invoices with their taxes; the :guilabel:`Summary` tab totals them per tax. Click :guilabel:`View Issued Invoices` or :guilabel:`View Received Invoices` to display the books. Click :guilabel:`Export draft` to download them as an XLSX file; after :guilabel:`Confirm`, the final file is downloaded with :guilabel:`Export BOE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:534
msgid "Under the :ref:`cash accounting regime <localizations/spain/cash-accounting>`, the invoices with VAT due on payment are booked once, on the day of the invoice, and their collections and payments are recorded in the *Cobro/Pago (Operación Criterio de Caja)* columns of the XLSX file (RIVA art. 61 decies): one row per collection or payment, with its date, its amount, the means and the account. The first one is on the row of the invoice, the following ones on additional rows that repeat the identification of the invoice. Refunds give negative amounts. The means use the codes of the AEAT format: 01 transfer, 02 cheque, 03 not collected or paid (the accrual on 31 December of the following year), 04 other means (including an invoice reconciled with a refund) and 05 direct debit. The entries that accrue the VAT are not booked as invoices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:547
msgid "Official annual accounts (PGC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/aeat_declarations.rst:549
