#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:5
msgid "Cash accounting regime (RECC) in Spain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:7
msgid "Under the Spanish **cash accounting regime** (*régimen especial del criterio de caja*, RECC), the output VAT of a sale is due, and the input VAT of a purchase is deductible, when the invoice is collected or paid, and at the latest on **31 December of the year following the operation** (LIVA arts. 163 decies to sexiesdecies). The ordinary rule is the opposite: VAT is due when the invoice is issued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:13
msgid "The Spanish localization (*Spain - Accounting (PGCE 2008)*, `l10n_es`) supports the regime for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:15
msgid "**companies under the regime**: their domestic sales and purchases follow the cash accounting rules;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:17
msgid "**companies under the general regime that buy from a supplier under the regime**: they deduct the VAT of that supplier's invoices when they pay them (LIVA art. 163 quinquiesdecies)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:21
msgid "Odoo does not check that the company meets the conditions to opt for the regime, or that the option has been communicated to the tax agency. Confirm with your tax advisor before enabling it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:25
msgid "The regime works with the Spanish charts of accounts of mainland Spain. It is not available for the Canary Islands charts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:29
msgid "Enable the regime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:31
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings` and scroll to the :guilabel:`Spain` section. The section is only shown for companies whose country is Spain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:33
msgid "In the :guilabel:`VAT regime` setting, select :guilabel:`Cash accounting (RECC)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:44
msgid "The :guilabel:`VAT regime` can also be chosen in the :ref:`Spanish company setup wizard <localizations/spain/setup-wizard>` (step :guilabel:`3. Tax regime`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:47
msgid "When the regime is saved for a company, Odoo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:49
msgid "activates the **RECC taxes** (see below);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:50
msgid "enables the cash basis feature of the Accounting settings, if it is not enabled yet, and sets the tax cash basis journal of the company if there is none;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:52
msgid "creates the RECC taxes and the two transition accounts if the company was created before this feature existed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:58
msgid "RECC taxes and transition accounts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:60
msgid "For each ordinary domestic VAT tax at 4 %, 10 % and 21 %, the localization provides a **twin tax** named like the ordinary tax followed by *RECC*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:63
msgid "sales: goods and services at 4 %, 10 % and 21 %;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:64
msgid "purchases: current goods, services and investment goods at 4 %, 10 % and 21 %."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:66
msgid "The twin taxes are identical to the ordinary ones (same rate, same tags in the tax report, so they are reported in the same boxes of the declarations), except that their :guilabel:`Tax Exigibility` is :guilabel:`Based on Payment` and that they use a **transition account**. They are loaded **inactive** (archived) and are activated when the company opts for the regime. You find them in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Taxes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:78
msgid "Used by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:79
msgid "477900 (4779)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:80
msgid "Output VAT pending accrual (cash accounting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:81
msgid "Sales RECC taxes: the VAT of a sale stays here until it is collected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:82
msgid "472900 (4729)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:83
msgid "Input VAT pending deduction (cash accounting)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:84
msgid "Purchase RECC taxes: the VAT of a purchase stays here until it is paid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:86
msgid "The Spanish names of the accounts are *Hacienda Pública. IVA repercutido pendiente de devengo (criterio de caja)* and *Hacienda Pública. IVA soportado pendiente de deducir (criterio de caja)*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:90
msgid "Sales and purchases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:92
msgid "Once the regime is enabled, you work as usual. When taxes are computed on an invoice line, and again when the invoice is posted, Odoo replaces the ordinary domestic VAT tax by its RECC twin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:95
msgid "on **customer invoices and vendor bills** of a company under the regime;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:96
msgid "on **vendor bills** from a supplier flagged as being under the regime (see :ref:`below <localizations/spain/cash-accounting/supplier>`), even if the company itself is under the general regime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:100
msgid "Only the taxes that have a twin are replaced. The **excluded operations** keep their own taxes: intra-community acquisitions, reverse charge operations, exports, the equivalence surcharge, and any other tax without a RECC twin (for example other rates, exempt operations or withholdings)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:105
msgid "The replacement only applies to invoices that are posted after the regime is enabled. Invoices that were already posted keep their ordinary taxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:109
msgid "Collection and payment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:111
msgid "When an invoice with RECC taxes is posted, its VAT is booked to the transition account. Each payment (partial or total) then generates an entry in the **tax cash basis journal** that moves the proportional part of the VAT from the transition account to the ordinary VAT account: 477 for the output VAT and 472 for the input VAT. The tax report tags are on this entry, so the VAT is reported in the period of the payment date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/cash_accounting.rst:117
msgid "Example: an invoice of 1,000.00 € with 21 % VAT (total 1,210.00 €) issued on 10 March 2025, of which 605.00 € (half) are collected on 10 May 2025."
msgstr ""

