#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:3
msgid "Spanish fixed assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:5
msgid "The *Spain - Fixed Assets* module adds the Spanish depreciation rules to the :doc:`asset management <../../accounting/vendor_bills/assets>` of the Accounting app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:8
msgid "three Spanish depreciation methods on asset categories and assets: straight line over the useful life, fixed annual percentage (official coefficient tables) and declining balance;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:10
msgid "a depreciation start date, for assets that are put into use after their purchase date;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:11
msgid "depreciation periods that follow the calendar, with the first period prorated by days;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:12
msgid "the non-deductible VAT and the VAT prorata part of the vendor bill line included in the value of the assets created from vendor bills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:16
msgid "The module is part of the :ref:`supported combination of Spanish modules <localizations/spain/module-choice>` and is installed with the :ref:`fiscal profile <localizations/spain/fiscal-profile>` when it is available on the server. It depends on the *Odoo 18 Assets Management* module and on *AEAT Base*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:20
msgid "The alternative community fixed asset modules (*Assets Management* and its Spanish version) cannot be installed together with it: Odoo refuses the installation, also from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:23
msgid "The Spanish rules only apply to assets. Deferred revenues keep the standard depreciation engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:29
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Management --> Asset Category` and open or create a category. In the depreciation settings of the category, select the :guilabel:`Spanish Depreciation Method`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:33
msgid ":guilabel:`Linear (useful life)`: the depreciable value is spread evenly over the useful life, which is the number of depreciations multiplied by the number of months between two depreciations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:36
msgid ":guilabel:`Fixed annual percentage`: every year, the :guilabel:`Annual Depreciation Percentage` of the depreciable value is depreciated (use the percentage of the official depreciation coefficient tables)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`Declining balance`: every year, the :guilabel:`Annual Depreciation Percentage` of the remaining value is depreciated. The remaining value is depreciated in full in the last period of the useful life."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:43
msgid "Leave the :guilabel:`Spanish Depreciation Method` empty to use the standard depreciation engine described in :doc:`../../accounting/vendor_bills/assets`. When a Spanish method is selected, the standard :guilabel:`Computation Method`, :guilabel:`Degressive Factor` and :guilabel:`Prorata Temporis` fields are hidden, as the Spanish method replaces them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:48
msgid "The :guilabel:`Annual Depreciation Percentage` is required for the fixed annual percentage and the declining balance methods; it must be greater than 0 and at most 100."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:51
msgid "With a Spanish method, the number of months between two depreciations (:guilabel:`One Entry Every`) must be 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 or 12, so that the periods fit into a calendar year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:57
msgid "Depreciation periods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:59
msgid "The :guilabel:`Depreciate to Period End` option (enabled by default) determines how the depreciation periods are counted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:62
msgid "**Enabled**: the periods follow the calendar (month, quarter, half-year or fiscal year, according to the number of months between two depreciations). The first period is prorated by days from the depreciation start date, and every depreciation line is dated on the last day of its period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:65
msgid "**Disabled**: the periods are counted from the depreciation start date and are never prorated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:78
msgid "When an asset is created with a category, it takes over the Spanish depreciation settings of the category. On a draft asset, the settings can also be changed directly: go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Management --> Assets`, open the asset, and adjust the :guilabel:`Spanish Depreciation Method`, the :guilabel:`Annual Depreciation Percentage` and the :guilabel:`Depreciate to Period End` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:84
msgid "If the asset is put into use later than its purchase date, fill in the :guilabel:`Depreciation Start Date` (the date the asset is available for use). The depreciation is then computed from this date instead of the asset :guilabel:`Date`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:88
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Compute Depreciation` to compute the depreciation board with the Spanish rules. The lines that are already posted are kept; only the lines that are not posted yet are recomputed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:92
msgid "The Spanish settings of an asset can only be changed while the asset is in draft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/fixed_assets.rst:97
msgid "When an asset is created from a vendor bill line with an asset category, its value includes the part of the VAT of the line that is not deductible: the non-deductible VAT and, for companies applying the VAT prorata, the non-deductible part of the prorata. These amounts are taken from the AEAT tax information of the bill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:5
msgid "With the :ref:`Spanish fiscal profile <localizations/spain/fiscal-profile>` and its :guilabel:`SII Taxpayer` option, the SII (*Llevanza de libros registro del IVA a través de la Sede electrónica de la AEAT*) is handled by the *Suministro Inmediato de Información en el IVA* module. It sends the VAT data of customer invoices and vendor bills to the web service of the AEAT, or of the regional tax agency of the company. The SII is mandatory for companies with a turnover above 6 M€, for the taxpayers registered in the REDEME, and optional for the others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:13
msgid "The standard *Spain - SII EDI Suministro de Libros* module described in :ref:`the SII section of the Spain page <localizations/spain/sii>` cannot be installed together with *AEAT Base*, which the fiscal profile installs (see :ref:`localizations/spain/module-choice`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:20
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`SII Taxpayer` in the :ref:`fiscal profile <localizations/spain/fiscal-profile>` (:menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, :guilabel:`Spain` section) and save, or select :guilabel:`SII taxpayer` in step :guilabel:`2. Fiscal profile` of the :ref:`company setup wizard <localizations/spain/setup-wizard>`. Odoo installs the SII module and its extensions: the OSS operations, the matching of the invoices with the AEAT records, and the summary of the simplified invoices of the Point of Sale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:28
msgid "A company cannot use the SII and Veri*Factu at the same time: SII taxpayers are exempt from Veri*Factu. When you choose :guilabel:`SII (immediate supply of information)` in step :guilabel:`4. Invoicing mode` of the wizard, the wizard turns Veri*Factu off, and enables the SII in the test environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:37
msgid "Certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/spain/sii.rst:39
msgid "The requests are signed with the electronic certificate of the company (a :file:`.p12` or :file:`.pfx` file)."
